\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 South Korea \highlight\uc2  won cuts losses as  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  cited\b0\par\par\uc2 357 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2008\par 01:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to midday)\par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Dec 2 (Reuters) - The South Korean won cut much of its early losses of up to 2.9 percent against the dollar on Tuesday as some traders saw dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities and on exporter demand for settlements.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also injected all of a planned $4 billion into local banks using its dollar credit line at the U.S. Federal Reserve for the first time, helping easing their dollar funding shortages. [ID:nSEL000381]\par \par \uc2 Still, the won <KRW=> remained under pressure from fresh worries about a slowdown in Asia's fourth-largest economy amid a global recession.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at 1,457.9/8.6 per dollar as of 0245 GMT, compared with Monday's domestic close <KRW=KFTC> of 1,440.0. It slid to as low as 1,482.9.\par \par \uc2 "The authorities kept supporting the won on the quiet, but we cannot rule out the possibility of the won's further fall," said a dealer at a foreign bank.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, a deputy finance minister said the country might need to cut its economic growth forecast for the next year, just after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  revised down its third quarter growth figures.\par \par \uc2 Seoul shares <.KS11> fell 2.69 percent as foreign investors sold a net 4.9 billion won worth of stocks in the country's main exchange.\par \par \uc2 Foreigners bought a combined net 622.7 billion won during the last four consecutive sessions, the longest net foreign buying streak since early June. So far this year foreign investors have sold a net 34.4 trillion won of South Korean shares.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                       0245 GMT      0020 GMT    prev close\par  Won <KRW=>           1,457.9/8.6   1,468.4/9.1       1,440.0\par  Yen/won <JPYKRW=R>    15.5663/20    15.6892/40    15.1155/28\par  KOSPI <.KS11>           1,030.18      1,015.44      1,058.62\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Cheon Jong-woo and Lee Kyoung-ho; Editing by Jonathan Hopfner)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081205e4c20001x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
