\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea won down on President; \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  spotted\b0\par\par\uc2 By Cheon Jong-woo   \par \uc2 574 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Oktober 2008\par 02:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2    (Updates to domestic close)\par \par \uc2  SEOUL, Oct 21 (Reuters) - The South Korean won fell slightly against the dollar on Tuesday after bleak remarks about Asia's fourth-largest economy from President Lee Myung-bak and on persistent worries about money supply in local financial markets.\par \par \uc2  The won <KRW=> also came under pressure from weaker stocks and on dollar demand from importers, despite measures from the country, the second bailout package this week, to help ailing construction sectors and to stabilise financial markets.\par \par \uc2  The local unit recovered some of its earlier losses as the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities were spotted selling dollars to cut the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's falls, but the move failed to lift it as trading was too thin, analysts said.\par \par \uc2  The South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to remain under pressure from lingering worries about a slowdown in the global economy, although eased concerns over the credit crisis after Sunday's $130 billion South Korean financial rescue package may give some relief to the won, analysts said.\par \par \uc2  "Concerted actions by the global authorities have relieved investors a bit, but nobody thinks the world is free from the sluggish economy and the credit crunch," said Jeong My-young, an analyst at Samsung Futures Inc.\par \par \uc2  "The won is seen moving around the 1,300 (per dollar) for a while, but it is more likely to weaken further than to rebound," she added.\par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at 1,320.0/0/.4 per dollar as of 0600 GMT, compared with Monday's domestic close <KRW=KFTC> of 1,315.\par \par \uc2  Reflecting concerns over the short-term liquidity at banks and companies, prices of the country's two main 91-day debt instruments fell further, bucking treasury bonds' rally.\par \par \uc2  South Korean President Lee Myung-bak said the economic situation was more serious than during the Asian financial crisis 10 years ago because of a looming global economic recession, according to the presidential spokesman.\par \par \uc2  Seoul shares <.KS11> ended down 0.0.95 percent after rising as much as 2.18 percent as foreign investors sold a net 149 million won worth of stocks in the country's main exchange, much less than in recent sessions.\par \par \uc2  Foreigners dumped 1.91 trillion won in South Korean stocks during the previous four consecutive sessions.\par \par \uc2  That forced the won to slid to as low as 1,335.9.\par \par \uc2  Dollar spot trade volume was just $2.53 billion, less than a third of the year's daily average trading volume of $8.88 billion, according to data from Seoul Money Brokerage Service Ltd and Korea money Broker Corp.\par \par \uc2  Investors have become reluctant to trade in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as the authorities have kept warning against speculative trading, which in turn has the effect of making the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  less effective, analysts said.\par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had provided $1.52 billion out of the previously planned $2.5 billion in three-month swap deals to local banks. [ID:nSEO338532]\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                       0600 GMT     0305 GMT   prev close\par  Won <KRW=>           1,320.0/0.4  1,326.4/9.1      1,315.0\par  Yen/won <JPYKRW=R>    12.9860/02   13.0267/72   12.8722/80\par  KOSPI <.KS11>           1,196.10     1,213.67     1,207.63\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  (Editing by Keiron Henderson)\par \par \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081024e4al00035\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
