\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED - CORRECTED-S.Korea won at 4-yr low despite warning\b0\par\par\uc2 By Cheon Jong-woo   \par \uc2 562 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 2008\par 12:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Corrects story to make clear the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was minor and a regular market smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that some dealers said they had not detected such sales)\par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Sept 2 (Reuters) - The South Korean won fell 1.6 percent to hit a nearly four-year low against the dollar on Tuesday, despite official warnings of stern measures in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 Some dealers said the authorities were seen selling a small amount of dollars, but this was seen as a regular market smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  rather than an attempt to affect \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels.\par \par \uc2 The reported dollar-selling, which other dealers said they had not detected, was too weak anyhow to absorb dollar bids from importers and foreign investors who kept selling Seoul shares with the local stock hitting a 18-month low.\par \par \uc2 The won <KRW=> is expected to slide further, despite possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the authorities, on lingering concerns over capital outflow from the country and a slowdown in Asia's fourth-largest economy, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "It is a matter of time for the won to weaken to 1,140 (per dollar) and it may fall further to 1,200. Some expect the won to rebound once concerns over the September financial crisis get resolved, but even after that, we will still have bearish factors such as global credit crunch and economic slowdown," said Jeong My-young, an analyst at Samsung Futures Inc.\par \par \uc2 The authorities have few other options but to resume massive dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the won, but then that could fuel concerns about \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, she added.\par \par \uc2 Dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually results in lower \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell $4.32 billion in August after suffering a record loss in the previous month, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed earlier.\par \par \uc2 The South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at 1,133.4/4.1 per dollar as of 0600 GMT, compared with Monday's domestic close of 1,116 <KRW=KFTC>.\par \par \uc2 The won fell to as low as 1,133.9, the weakest since Oct. 26, 2004, just before the local market closed.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, it rose to as high as 1,108.3 after Vice Finance Minister Kim Dong-soo said the country had both the will and the ability to deal with one-way bets against the won, and called for calm a day after local financial markets tumbled on fears of massive capital flight out of the country. [ID:nSEO66739]\par \par \uc2 Investors have been worried that a huge amount of domestic bonds coming due next week would spur capital outflows.\par \par \uc2 South Korean shares <.KS11> ended at their lowest close in 18 months as foreign investors sold a net 264.1 billion won worth of stocks in the country's main exchange.\par \par \uc2 They unloaded a combined net 2.26 trillion won during the previous 10 consecutive sessions.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                       0600 GMT     0250 GMT   prev close\par  Won <KRW=>           1,133.4/4.1  1,118.9/9.4        1,116\par  Yen/won <JPYKRW=R>    10.4886/09   10.3344/18   10.2829/76\par  KOSPI <.KS11>           1,407.14     1,418.69     1,414.43\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Lee Kyoung-ho; Editing by Jonathan Thatcher)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 3, CORRECTED)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080905e492000vz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
