\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX- \highlight22\uc2 South Korea \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions \highlight\uc2  in past 12 months\b0\par\par\uc2 633 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 September 2008\par 11:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * For a related story, double-click [ID:nSEO101474\par \par \uc2 Sept 1 (Reuters) - The South Korean authorities have sold more than $30 billion in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets this year to prop up the won and fight imported inflation, estimates by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers compiled by Reuters show.\par \par \uc2 South Korea has removed almost all \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls since the 1997-98 Asia financial crisis but it has frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, sometimes verbally, sometimes by directly selling or buying \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The country's authorities normally do not confirm their market \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  or comment on their size.\par \par \uc2 Following are key dates in the past year when dealers have reported the authorities buying or selling dollars against the won, or when policymakers issued remarks aimed at influencing the exchange rate:\par \par \uc2 Sept. 1, 2008 - Won tumbles 3 percent to hit a fresh near four-year low although the authorities are seen selling small amounts of dollars and warn of action.\par \par \uc2 Aug. 29, 2008 - Won falls although the authorities are seen selling a small amount of dollars.\par \par \uc2 Aug. 28, 2008 - Won slightly rises on reported dollar selling and vice finance minister's warning of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Aug. 27, 2008 - Won rises on reported \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and official warnings.\par \par \uc2 Aug. 22, 2008 - Won hits a near four-year low although the authorities are estimated to have sold some $2 billion.\par \par \uc2 Aug. 21, 2008 - Won falls although the authorities are seen selling small amounts of dollars.\par \par \uc2 Aug. 20, 2008 - Won steadies as the authorities are estimated to have sold up to $800 million.\par \par \uc2 Aug. 14, 2008 - Won falls although the authorities are seen selling dollars.\par \par \uc2 Aug. 12, 2008 - Won falls although the authorities are seen selling dollars.\par \par \uc2 Aug. 11, 2008 - Won cuts losses as the authorities are estimated to have sold up to $2 billion.\par \par \uc2 Aug. 8, 2008 - Won falls over 1 percent although the authorities issue warnings and are seen selling dollars.\par \par \uc2 Aug. 5, 2008 - Won steadies as the authorities are seen selling dollars.\par \par \uc2 Aug. 4, 2008 - Won falls and the authorities are seen selling dollars.\par \par \uc2 July 31, 2008 - Won rises, authorities seen selling some $1 billion.\par \par \uc2 July 11-28 - Authorities seen selling a small amount of dollars in at least 11 sessions, whenever the won weakens sharply.\par \par \uc2 July 10, 2008 - Won rises slightly, authorities seen selling a small amount of dollars. One-month won offshore forward contracts rise overnight and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  cited.\par \par \uc2 July 9, 2008 - Won hits its highest in over two months; authorities seen selling about $5 billion -- a record amount for one day -- and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials issue multiple warnings of measures to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 July 8, 2008 - Won hits a two-week high; authorities seen selling about $2 billion.\par \par \uc2 July 7, 2008 - Finance ministry and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  say in a joint statement they will take aggressive, concerted action and sell dollars when necessary to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 July 2, 2008 - Won soars 2 percent from a session low; authorities seen selling $3 billion; a finance ministry official warns of action to stabilise the market.\par \par \uc2 June 2008 - Authorities seen selling about $5 billion in total during the month, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on at least five days.\par \par \uc2 May 2008 - Authorities seen selling about $3 billion in May, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on at least two days.\par \par \uc2 April 2008 - Authorities seen buying a small amount of dollars.\par \par \uc2 March 2008 - Authorities seen selling about $1 billion on March 18 to support the won, but buying about $800 million on March 26 to send the won down.\par \par \uc2 October 2007 - Authorities spotted buying more than $1 billion before and after the won rises to 10-year highs on at least four days. (Writing by Cheon Jong-woo and Yoo Choonsik in SEOUL)\par \par \uc2 KOREA-ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (FACTBOX)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|ABX|BNX|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080901e4910019k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
