\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia rangebound; c.banks shore up won, rupiah\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kevin Yao   \par \uc2 803 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 2008\par 06:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 8 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved in tight ranges on Tuesday with investor sentiment torn between falling oil prices and renewed credit fears, while authorities in \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Indonesia \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  The won <KRW=> hit a two-week high at 1,025.3 per dollar, up 1.7 percent from Monday's domestic close of 1,042.9, as dealers said authorities sold up to $2 billion to boost the local unit.\par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, traders also cited dollar-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try to support the rupiah <IDR=>.\par \par \uc2  "Bank Indonesia is still on the offer side," said a trader in Jakarta. "It seems that they are trying to push the dollar below 9,200."\par \par \uc2  A second trader said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was aimed at keeping the rupiah in tight ranges.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed the rupiah <IDR=> as high as 9,190 per dollar before it edged back to around 9,205.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has gained about 1 percent against the dollar in the past month, benefiting from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's three successive interest rate rises since early May, which took the benchmark rate to 8.75 percent, among the highest in Asia.\par \par \uc2  Standard Chartered expects the Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> to trade near 9,200 per dollar at the end of September before rising to 9,150 by the end of 2008, analysts at the bank said in a note, raising their forecast from 9,250 and 9,200, respectively.\par \par \uc2  "Bank Indonesia is committed to raise interest rates gradually which should mitigate capital outflows," the analysts said, adding that the rupiah could hit 9,100 by end-March 2009 and 9,000 by end-June.\par \par \uc2  Several authorities in Asia have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent months to support their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as part of efforts to cushion rising import prices from the likes of surging oil.\par \par \uc2  WEAKER PESO\par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso <PHP=> pulled back to 45.88 per dollar, down a third of a percent from Monday's close to its weakness level since September, after briefly hitting as high as 45.63.\par \par \uc2  Traders said buying interest in the peso was undermined by concerns about high oil prices and the global credit crisis.\par \par \uc2  "The bullish sentiment (on the dollar versus the peso) is still intact, it seems a test of the 46 level is just around the corner," said a trader in Manila.\par \par \uc2  A second trader added: "Oil prices are still above $140 and (domestic) inflation is getting higher and higher."\par \par \uc2  Oil prices <CLc1> held largely steady on Tuesday after dropping close to $4 on Monday, backing off last week's record high of $145.85.\par \par \uc2  On Monday, a \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2  report said a pending accounting change could force Fannie Mae  and \uc2 Freddie Mac\uc2  , the top U.S. mortgage funders, to raise a combined $75 billion in capital at a tough time. [ID:nN07435475]\par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Pakistani rupee was 2.9 percent weaker at a record low of 73 to the dollar <PKR=PK> because of worries about inflation, widening current and budget account deficits and security, dealers said.\par \par \uc2  The rupee had closed at 71.00/05 to the dollar on Monday.\par \par \uc2  The rupee has lost more than 18 percent against the dollar this year as annual inflation accelerated to a three-decade high of 19.27 percent in May and fiscal and current account deficits widened.  \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day at  0748 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       106.55         107.65       +1.03\par  Sing dlr        1.3609         1.3643       +0.25\par  Taiwan dlr      30.397         30.399       +0.01\par  Korean won     1032.50        1039.00       +0.63\par  Baht             33.67          33.66       -0.03\par  Peso             45.88          45.72       -0.35\par  Rupiah         9201.00        9202.00       +0.01\par  Rupee            43.36          43.29       -0.17\par  Ringgit         3.2610         3.2645       +0.11\par  Yuan            6.8545         6.8690       +0.21\par  Change so far in 2008\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       106.55         111.33       +4.49\par  Sing dlr        1.3609         1.4382       +5.68\par  Taiwan dlr      30.397         32.443       +6.73\par  Korean won     1032.50         935.70       -9.38\par  Baht             33.67          33.68       +0.03\par  Peso             45.88          41.28      -10.03\par  Rupiah         9201.00        9390.00       +2.05\par  Rupee            43.36          39.41       -9.11\par  Ringgit         3.2610         3.3050       +1.35\par  Yuan            6.8545         7.3041       +6.56\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  (Editing by Jacqueline Wong)\par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \hi