\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 2-S.Korea gears up for  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  fight, sells $5 bln\b0\par\par\uc2 By Cheon Jong-woo and Yoo Choonsik   \par \uc2 862 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juli 2008\par 01:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments)\par \par \uc2 SEOUL, July 9 (Reuters) - South Korea geared up for a fight with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, warning on Wednesday it would not let the won weaken beyond 1,000 per dollar after its biggest one-day sale of dollars on record.\par \par \uc2 Dealers estimated South Korea dumped around $5 billion on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday alone, propelling the won to its strongest intraday rise in a decade as part of a strategy to prevent the weakness seen in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far this year from fuelling inflation.\par \par \uc2 A senior \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that authorities would not allow the won to weaken beyond 1,000 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell 10.5 percent against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first half of the year, exacerbating the impact on domestic inflation of rising imports costs for oil and other raw materials.\par \par \uc2 "The won can't be said to be at a 'balanced level' when it is traded at a four-digit rate per dollar," Rhee Gwang-ju, a deputy governor at the Bank of Korea, told Reuters in a telephone interview.\par \par \uc2 "(The authorities) have no reason to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  even if the won strengthens to a three-digit rate."\par \par \uc2 Dealers estimate that South Korean authorities have now sold about $17 billion this year to prop up the won, which has ranged between 1,057 per dollar and 930 per dollar so far in 2008.\par \par \uc2 Dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at offsetting imported inflation has persuaded economists that the Bank of Korea will refrain from raising rates when it meets on Thursday and will instead keep them on hold for the 11th consecutive month.\par \par \uc2 BIGGEST ONE-DAY GAIN IN DECADE\par \par \uc2 The won rose as much as 3.7 percent on the day, its biggest intraday gain against the dollar since March 23, 1998, as dealers reported the authorities sold dollars for won right after an official issued a fresh warning against betting on a weaker unit.\par \par \uc2 The surge in the won <KRW=> <KRW=KFTC> sent bond futures prices sharply higher as traders became more convinced monetary authorities would stick to using the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as its main tool to rein in inflation, rather than interest rates.\par \par \uc2 The won rose to as high as 996.0 per dollar, the strongest bid since 991.75 on April 29, helping to drive September treasury bond futures <KTBc1> up by as much as 38 ticks on the day.\par \par \uc2 But concern a stronger won will reduce the country's exports potential hit share prices in electronics makers. The sector's index <.KS41> fell 2.65 percent.\par \par \uc2 The reported dollar sales came right after a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  official warned against those who doubt South Korea's capability to dominate what they call speculative traders.\par \par \uc2 "Efforts by the government and the Bank of Korea to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate don't stop here," said the official, who declined to be identified.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data backs up an estimate by dealers that \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  has drawn down billions of dollars for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, a war chest amounting to nearly $260 billion.\par \par \uc2 IMPACT ON EXPORTERS\par \par \uc2 South Korea's annual consumer inflation hit a near 10-year high of 5.5 percent in June and producer inflation data released on Wednesday indicated there was further inflationary pressure in the pipeline.\par \par \uc2 The producer price index grew 10.5 percent in June over a year earlier, the fastest annual gain since November 1998, data from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed.\par \par \uc2 For a graphic on South Korean inflation data, click: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://customers.reuters.com/d/graphics/KR_PPI0708.gif"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://customers.reuters.com/d/graphics/KR_PPI0708.gif}}}\par \par \uc2 Reflecting pressure on the won, the government expects the country to record its first trade deficit this year since the 1997 Asian financial crisis because of the rising cost of imports.\par \par \uc2 But the falling share prices of \uc2 Samsung Electronics\uc2  and other electronics makers in response to the won's jump underscored how easily a policy can damage another part of Asia's fourth-largest economy.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came just hours after senior officials from the government, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and financial regulator held a hastily arranged meeting and called on stock investors not to panic.\par \par \uc2 "The government has (treated) the major economic problems facing Korea with a succession of short-term band-aid solutions that haven't amounted to much at all," said Daniel Melser, an economist at \uc2 Moody's\uc2  Economy.com.\par \par \uc2 "The lack of a consistent and cohesive approach to macroeconomic policy has eroded confidence in the administration and the country," he added. For related stories, double-click: * [ID:nSEO357134] for interview story with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official * [ID:nSEO90043] for story on efforts to calm stock markets * [ID:nSEO349204] for story on possible easing in borrowing * [ID:nSEO56119] for a poll on Thursday's rate meeting (Additional reporting by Lee Shin-hyung and Lee Jin-joo; editing by Keiron Henderson and Neil Fullick)\par \par \uc2 KOREA-ECONOMY/ (WRAPUP 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|O|OIL|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|J|RNP|DNP|PCM|PEN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080708e47800001\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
