\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For July 8\b0\par\par\uc2 2,520 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 2008\par 09:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SOUTH KOREA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  WON SURGES ON SUSPECTED GOVERNMENT \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The won rose sharply after traders said the South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in both the domestic market Tuesday and the offshore non-deliverable market overnight to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0150 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIA ECON SLOWDOWN PRONOUNCED; BUSINESS SLUMPS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The trickle of information that a few months ago began pointing to a slowdown in the Australian economy has now become a torrent after business conditions plunged in June, further cutting the risk that interest rates will need to be raised again. (published 0614 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =3RD UPDATE:GRIM NZ BUSINESS CONFIDENCE PUTS JUL EASING IN PLAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's business confidence remained at a 34-year low in the second quarter, confirming recessionary economic conditions which leaves the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  poised to embark on rate cuts, possibly as early as this month. (published 0440 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN ECON WATCHERS SURVEY SHOWS WORKERS PESSIMISM INCREASING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Workers on the front lines of Japan's economy were increasingly pessimistic about current and future economic conditions due to higher oil and material prices in June, a government survey showed Tuesday. (published 0643 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN JUN BANK LENDING GROWTH FASTEST IN 2 YRS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Lending by Japanese banks grew at its fastest pace in almost two years in June on increased corporate fund demand, while growth in money supply accelerated. (published 0217 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN JUNE 1-20 TRADE DEFICIT Y230.43 BILLION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan posted a merchandise trade deficit of Y230.43 billion in the first 20 days of June, compared with a Y448.83 surplus in the year-earlier period, the Finance Ministry said Tuesday. (published 0010 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN JUNE CORP BANKRUPTCY CASES UP 8.1% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese corporate bankruptcies rose 8.1% in June to 1065 cases, private credit research agency Teikoku Databank Ltd. said Tuesday. (published 0430 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: 5-YR JGB AUCTION STRONG AS SENTIMENT IMPROVES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Demand was strong at an auction of five-year Japanese government bonds Tuesday, as faltering share prices and receding expectations for an interest rate hike boosted the bonds' attractiveness. (published 0535 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDONESIA ECONOMY MAY GROW BELOW 6.2% TARGET FOR 2008-FIN MIN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indonesian economy may grow below an initial target of 6.2% this year because of to high inflation, Finance Minister Sri Mulyani Indrawati told reporters Tuesday. (published 0430 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S&P: S KOREA ECONOMY TO GROW 4.3% THIS YEAR VS +5.0% IN 2007 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A senior analyst at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ratings Services said Tuesday he forecasts South Korean economic growth of 4.3% this year, lower than the 5.0% expansion recorded in 2007. (published 0547 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA AIMS TO UP 2012 HANDSET EXPORTS TO $70B VS $29B '07 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea is targeting to raise its exports of mobile phones to $70 billion in 2012 from $29 billion in 2007, the Ministry of Knowledge Economy said Tuesday. (published 0215 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par G8 EXPRESSES "STRONG CONCERN" ABOUT HIGHER OIL, FOOD PRICES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Leaders from the Group of Eight leading industrialized nations Tuesday expressed "strong concern" about threats being posed by rising oil and food prices to the world's economy. (published 0544 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MALAYSIA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO SELL MYR3.5B FEB 2018 MGS JULY 14 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  plans to auction MYR3.5 billion of February 2018 Malaysian Government Securities, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on its Web site Tuesday. (published 0323 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ST GEORGE BANK\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO SELL A$506M ABS - MARKET SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 St. George Bank Ltd.\f28 \uc2 \f2  plans to sell A$506 million in asset-backed securities, a market participant who had seen the term sheet said Tuesday. (published 0447 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TELECOM CORP OF NEW ZEALAND\f28 \uc2 \f2  PRICES CHF200M SWISS BOND ISSUE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Telecom Corp. of New Zealand\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday it has priced a CHF200 million Swiss bond issue, the proceeds from which will be used to refinance debt and general corporate purposes. (published 0348 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OCBC TO UNDERWRITE S$500M IN BONDS FOR SINGAPORE HDB -SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's Housing and Development Board has hired \f28 \uc2 \f2 Oversea-Chinese Banking Corp. Ltd.\f28 \uc2 \f2  to underwrite S$500 million in local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bonds, two people familiar with the matter said Tuesday. (published 0507 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par COMMODITIES BOOM TO INSULATE AUSTRALIAN ECONOMY -BIS SHRAPNEL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The global commodities boom will likely help insulate the Australian economy from recession over the next five years, although commodities prices are expected to trough in either 2010 or 2011, a report from BIS Shrapnel released Tuesday said. (published 0050 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIA MINIMUM WAGE RISE THREATENS ECONOMY -INDUS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Fair Pay Commission Tuesday agreed to raise the minimum wage by over 4% per week, prompting a warning from industry that the move could trigger an economy-wide price breakout as firms look to claw back higher wage costs. (published 0649 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINE FIN SECY: SCRAPPING VAT ON OIL TO COST PHP73.1B \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine Finance Secretary Margarito Teves Tuesday warned the government stands to lose PHP73.1 billion should lawmakers scrap the value-added tax on oil. (published 0219 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par VIETNAM JUNE NEW VEHICLE SALES UP 60% ON YR BUT FALL ON MONTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sales of new vehicles in Vietnam surged 60% on year in June, rising for the 23rd straight month. (published 0256 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ASIA: MONGOLIA TOGROG SET TO RISE MORE AS UNREST WINDS DN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Mongolian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  looks set to continue, or even accelerate, its steady climb against the U.S. dollar, driven by efforts to curb local inflation and as the recent wave of political violence winds down. (published 0510 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PREVIEW: CHINA JUN EXPORT, MONEY-SUPPLY GROWTH LIKELY SLOWED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese exports likely rose more slowly in June because weakening global economic growth hurt demand for China-made goods, economists said. (published 0358 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: KOREA'S INFLATION FIGHT STILL LACKS CONVICTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean authorities want us to think they are serious about their pledge to fight inflation and therefore support the won. Indeed, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has gained a fair bit in the past two days with the U.S. dollar down as low as KRW1,026, in part due to a burst of rhetoric and market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by government officials. (published 0127 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par =UPDATE: SINOSTEEL CLOSES IN ON MIDWEST CONTROL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sinosteel Corp.\f28 \uc2 \f2  was Tuesday closing in on winning control of its takeover target \f28 \uc2 \f2 Midwest Corp. Ltd.\f28 \uc2 \f2  but failed rival bidder Murchison Metals Group Ltd. has vowed it will not allow the Chinese metals trader to win 100% of the Australian iron ore developer. (published 0527 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TANGO EXTENDS HERALD RESOURCES BID, CONSIDERING OPTIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Tango consortium said Tuesday it is extending its A$553.6 million takeover offer for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Herald Resources Ltd.\f28 \uc2 \f2  to July 15 and is considering its options with regard to the bid. (published 0437 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ANTAM CONSIDERING OPTIONS ON HERALD; COULD RAISE OFFER - CEO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesian state nickel miner \f28 \uc2 \f2 PT Aneka Tambang\f28 \uc2 \f2 , or Antam, is considering its options in a takeover bid for Australian base metals developer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Herald Resources Ltd.\f28 \uc2 \f2  including raising its offer, Antam Chief Executive Alwin Syah Loebis told reporters Tuesday. (published 0640 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =NORTH ASIAN STOCK MARKETS LEAD REGION LOWER, BANKS WEAK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets are falling Tuesday in thin, skittish trade, with North Asian markets taking the biggest hit. (published 0554 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE:ARKMILE SEEKS MTG TO WIND UP CHALLENGER INFRA FUND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. property tycoon Vincent Tchenguiz's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Consensus Business Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  has asked Australia's Challenger Infrastructure Fund to hold a general meeting of unitholders that would consider winding up the fund. (published 0552 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: ALLCO SELLS PART OF SINGAPORE REAL ESTATE UNIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Embattled \f28 \uc2 \f2 Allco Finance Group Ltd.\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday it has sold part of its Singaporean real estate arm for S$180 million, or about A$138 million, to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Frasers Centrepoint Ltd.\f28 \uc2 \f2  (published 0024 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA COSCO: EXPECTS 1H NET PROFIT UP MORE THAN 90% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Cosco Holdings Co. said Tuesday it expects its unaudited first half net profit to increase by more than 90% from a year earlier due to a healthy international shipping industry and the company's improved management. (published 2313 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA MINSHENG BANKING:EXPECTS 1H NET PFT UP OVER 110% ON YR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Minsheng Banking Corp.\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday it expects its unaudited first-half net profit to rise by more than 110% from a year earlier on stable and rapid growth in its loan, investment and wealth management divisions. (published 2304 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 AIR CHINA\f28 \uc2 \f2 , CHINA SOUTHERN TO RAISE FUEL SURCHARGES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Air China Ltd.\f28 \uc2 \f2  and China Southern Airlines Co. said they will raise their fuel surcharges on international routes starting Thursday. (published 0338 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE:STANLEY HO'S SISTER SEEKS HK REVIEW OVER SJM LISTING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A Hong Kong court will convene Tuesday morning to decide on an application for a judicial review filed by tycoon Stanley Ho's sister Winnie Ho, who wants to stop the listing of the tycoon's casino flagship on the local bourse, which is scheduled for Thursday. (published 0310 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MAZDA PRES: NO PLAN TO CHANGE FY UNIT SALES PROJECTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mazda Motor Corp.\f28 \uc2 \f2  President Hisakazu Imaki said Tuesday that the company is sticking to its unit sales projection for this fiscal year, even as global auto market conditions remain severe due to surging gasoline prices, a gloomy world economy, and other factors. (published 0253 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FORD MOTOR CHINA: 1H SALES 172,133 UNITS; UP 21% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ford Motor Co.\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday its China \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold 172,133 vehicles in the first half of this year, up 21% from the same period a year earlier. (published 0241 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSENCO: FIRE AT EQUINOX COPPER PROJECT IN ZAMBIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 08-07-08 0712GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian mining contractor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ausenco Ltd.\f28 \uc2 \f2  said a fire at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Equinox Minerals Ltd.\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Lumwana copper project had damaged electricity equipment and will cause a delay in the mine's commissioning. (published 2301 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NZ'S OIL & GAS RAISES NZ$192.7M IN OPTIONS EXERCISE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand Oil & Gas\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday that a successful options exercise has provided the company with a capital injection of NZ$192.7 million that will be used to help pursue investment opportunities. (published 0005 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OLAM TO BUY 24.99% STAKE IN DAIRY TRUST FOR NZ$101M \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore-based commodities firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Olam International Ltd.\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday it will pay NZ$101.05 million for a 24.99% stake in New Zealand-based Dairy Trust Ltd. (published 0013 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TRANSURBAN: CITYLINK 4Q REVENUE UP 9.7% TO A$94.1M \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Transurban Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday that toll and fee revenue on its key Citylink tollroad in Melbourne rose 9.7% on anormalized basis to A$94.1 million during the three months to June from a year ago. (published 0107 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SEVEN & I MAR-MAY GROUP NET PROFIT Y33.1B VS Y35.7B \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese retail giant \f28 \uc2 \f2 Seven & I Holdings Co.\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday that its net profit for the fiscal first quarter to May fell 7.5% on year, partly hurt by weakness in its department store business and North American convenience store \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0640 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par OIL FUTURES: NYMEX CRUDE UP ON BARGAIN HUNTING; NO RALLY SEEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude oil futures spiked $1 a barrel Tuesday in Asia on bargain hunting following a steep overnight drop, but the market is expected to enter a consolidation phase rather than rally in the near term. (published 0703 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINOPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2 : HAINAN REFINERY BEGAN COMMERCIAL OPS JULY 1 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Petrochemical Corp.\f28 \uc2 \f2 , or Sinopec Group, said Tuesday it started commercial \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of its 160,000-barrel-a-day refinery in southern Hainan July 1. (published 0345 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 COSMO OIL\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO RESTART 130,000 B/D CHIBA CDU ON FRIDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cosmo Oil Co.\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday it will restart on July 11 the 130,000 barrel-a-day No. 2 crude distillation unit at its Chiba refinery east of Tokyo. (published 0333 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NANSEI SEKIYU:TO RESTART 100,000 B/D NISHIHARA REFINERY THUR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nansei Sekiyu KK\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday it will restart its sole Nishihara refinery on July 10 after the completion of regular maintenance. (published 0428 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TONENGENERAL WAKAYAMA REFINERY CLOSED DUE TO BAD WEATHER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TonenGeneral Sekiyu KK's 170,000 barrel-a-day Wakayama refinery in western Japan has been shut since this morning due to thunder in the area, an official of the local Arida City fire department said Tuesday. (published 0525 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SHELL PLANS TO BUILD STORAGE TANKS IN INDONESIA BY 1Q 2009 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Royal Dutch Shell Plc\f28 \uc2 \f2  plans to build its first terminal and six tanks in Indonesia to store fuels imported to meet the country's rising demand, a company spokeswoman said Tuesday. (published 0343 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINE FIN SECY: SCRAPPING VAT ON OIL TO COST PHP73.1B \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine Finance Secretary Margarito Teves Tuesday warned the government stands to lose PHP73.1 billion should lawmakers scrap the value-added tax on oil. (published 0219 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KOREA GAS JUNE LNG SALES DOWN 7.5% ON YR TO 1.42M TONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 State-run Korea Gas Corp., or Kogas, said Tuesday its domestic natural gas sales in June fell 7.5% on year to 1.42 million metric tons of liquefied natural gas because new coal-fired power generation facilities lowered demand for LNG for power generation. (published 0257 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par W AUSTRALIA KWINANA POWER STATION BACK IN SERVICE - GOVT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Verve Energy\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Kwinana power station is back in production after three months' maintenance, helping to offset the impact from the power shortage in Western Australia state following a major gas explosion in early June, the Western Australian government said Tuesday. (published 0157 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: CHALCO SLUMPS ON OUTPUT CUT AT TWO SHANXI PLANTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shares of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Aluminum Corp. of China Ltd.\f28 \uc2 \f2  slumped Tuesday after China's largest alumina producer by output said two of its aluminum smelters in Shanxi province have been forced to cut production because of a power shortage. (published 0605 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par VIETNAM OKS BUILDING OF 560,000-TON FERTILIZER PLANT BY 2010 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnamese Prime Minister Nguyen Tan Dung has approved the construction of a fertilizer plant with an annual capacity of 560,000 metric tons in Thanh Hoa province, the government said Tuesday. (published 0608 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par VALE KEEN TO EXPLORE MORE GOLD, COPPER, NICKEL IN PHILIPPINE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazil's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Companhia Vale do Rio Doce\f28 \uc2 \f2 , or Vale, is interested in exploring for copper, gold and nickel in three additional areas in the Philippines, the Mines and Geosciences Bureau said Tuesday. (published 0433 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TANGO EXTENDS HERALD RESOURCES BID, CONSIDERING OPTIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Tango consortium said Tuesday it is extending its A$553.6 million takeover offer for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Herald Resources Ltd.\f28 \uc2 \f2  to July 15 and is considering its options with regard to the bid. (published 0437 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SOUTH KOREA FEED COS MAY BUY WHEAT IN JULY ON HIGH CORN RATES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean millers who make animal and poultry feed may buy a few cargoes of feed wheat to substitute corn, which is more expensive, a grains buyer based in Seoul said Tuesday. (published 0535 GMT) [ 08-07-08 0712GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080708e478000cf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
