\par\par \b \uc2 REFILE-HIGHLIGHTS- \highlight22\uc2 South Korea \highlight\uc2  warns of strong  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 2008\par 04:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Refiles to add dropped word in last sentence)\par \par \uc2 * For a full story, double-click [ID:nSEV000437]\par \par \uc2 SEOUL, July 7 (Reuters) - South Korea's finance ministry and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warned on Monday they would carry out strong concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if necessary to support the won and cushion imported inflation.\par \par \uc2 Following are key remarks in the joint statement from the Ministry of Strategy and Finance and the Bank of Korea and their separate news conferences, translated and compiled by Reuters:\par \par \uc2 STATEMENT\par \par \uc2 "The government and the Bank of Korea are of the same opinion that stabilising the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was necessary and agreed to aggressively take concerted action toward it."\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities are worried about a herd behaviour in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and believe it is most desirable for such a phenomenon to be resolved by itself in the market."\par \par \uc2 "The authorities will closely watch trends in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  supply and demand and in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates, and will take strong measures if there are excessive imbalances."\par \par \uc2 CHOI JONG-KU, DIRECTOR-GENERAL, INTERNATIONAL FINANCE BUREAU, MINISTRY OF STRATEGY AND FINANCE\par \par \uc2 "The authorities will use \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves if necessary to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market."\par \par \uc2 "The most important thing at this moment is price stability. \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy has to be managed toward it."\par \par \uc2 "We have \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves sufficient to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market."\par \par \uc2 "We are also looking for ways to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market without using \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves."\par \par \uc2 AHN BYUNG-CHAN, DIRECTOR, INTERNATIONAL DEPARTMENT, BANK OF KOREA\par \par \uc2 "The dollar/won rate had no reason to rise this much if not for psychological factors betting on the pair's rise."\par \par \uc2 "I believe market players are well aware (of the fair level for the won)."\par \par \uc2 "I don't see any side-effects (from strong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) because the market will get stabilised if the sentiment for stronger dollar/won is removed." (Reporting by Cheon Jong-woo, Lee Jin-joo, Yoo Choonsik; Editing by Keiron Henderson)\par \par \uc2 KOREA-ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HIGHLIGHTS, REFILE)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|ABX|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080710e4770005e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
