\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-POLL-South Korea June inflation seen at near 10-yr high\b0\par\par\uc2 637 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juli 2008\par 00:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (This is a repeat of an earlier story ahead of Tuesday's data release)\par \par \uc2 * What: South Korea's June consumer price index\par \par \uc2 * When: Tuesday, July 1, at 1:30 p.m. (0430 GMT)\par \par \uc2 * Annual consumer inflation seen at near decade high in June\par \par \uc2 By Lee Jin-joo\par \par \uc2 SEOUL, June 27 (Reuters) - South Korea's annual consumer inflation is seen hitting a near decade-high in June, fuelled by high oil prices and a weaker won <KRW=> despite government efforts to boost the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a poll showed on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The median forecast of economists polled by Reuters was for the consumer price index in June to rise 5.4 percent from a year earlier, compared with a 4.9 percent rise in May.\par \par \uc2 The forecast for June marks the strongest growth since consumer prices rose 6.8 percent in November 1998, and breaches the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target range of 2.5-3.5 percent for the seventh consecutive month.\par \par \uc2 The median forecast of economists was for the CPI to rise a non-seasonally adjusted 0.5 percent in June from a month earlier, lower than 0.8 percent in May, although investors generally look to the annual rate as the key inflation gauge.\par \par \uc2 "Despite the government's efforts to abandon its previous stance of a softer local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and boost the won's strength to stabilise inflation, the won is staying at a low level due to global credit woes while oil prices are staying at record highs," said Kim Jong-su, economist at NH Investment and Securities.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's financial authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to strengthen the won earlier this month to contain soaring import costs.\par \par \uc2 A weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually exacerbates inflation by effectively making imported oil and raw materials even more expensive.\par \par \uc2 Industrial goods, including oil products, contribute 34 percent to South Korea's consumer inflation, according to data from the statistics agency.\par \par \uc2 "Inflation risks remain, but the government won't be able to keep up efforts to boost the won if the country's trade balance continues to post deficits," said Cheon Min-kyu, economist at Korea Investment and Securities.\par \par \uc2 South Korea's trade balance has remained in the red for all but one month since December last year due to higher raw material prices.\par \par \uc2 Swelling inflation pressure amid downside risks from a slowdown in the global economy also has the Bank of Korea caught between a rock and a hard place.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held interest rates steady for the 10th consecutive month at 5.00 percent in June, after raising them by a quarter percentage point each in July and August 2007.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  holds its next policy meeting to review interest rates on July 10. Forecasts for South Korea's June consumer price index:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                   Percent change from\par                            prev month    year earlier\par  DBS Bank                              ~             5.5\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2                            0.7             5.6\par  CJ Investment & Securities          0.5             5.4\par  Goodmorning Shinhan Securities      0.5             5.4\par  Hana Daetoo Securities              0.3             5.2\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hyundai Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2                   0.4             5.3\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Korea Investment & Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2        0.5             5.4\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kiwoom Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2                    0.3             5.2\par  Mirae Asset Securities              0.4             5.3\par  NH Investment & Securities          0.3             5.2\par  SC First Bank                       0.2             5.1\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 SK Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2                        0.5             5.4\par  Solomon Investment Securities       0.5             5.4\par  _______________________________________________________\par  Median                              0.5             5.4\par  Low                                 0.2             5.1\par  High                                0.7             5.6\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ~ no forecast (Additional reporting by Chang Tae-min and Lee Eun-yul; editing by Jonathan Hopfner and Jacqueline Wong) (jinjoo.lee@thomsonreuters.com; +82 2 3704 5648; Reuters Messaging: jinjoo.lee.reuters.com@reuters.net))\f28 \par \par \uc2 KOREA-ECONOMY/INFLATION (POLL, REPEAT)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080703e46u00362\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
