\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia mixed ahead of Fed, rupee up after rate rise\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kevin Yao   \par \uc2 760 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juni 2008\par 05:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, June 25 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  lacked clear direction on Wednesday as investors waited for an announcement on U.S. monetary policy later in the day, but the Indian rupee gained after interest rates were raised to fight inflation.\par \par \uc2 Trading in Asia was cautious after recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by some central banks,including those in \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Philippines, to support their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The rupee <INR=IN> hit a two-week high of 42.782 per dollar after India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its lending rate to its highest in six years and increased banks' reserve requirements. [ID:nBOM196971].\par \par \uc2 One rupee trader in Singapore said the rise in India's call money rates made it more expensive to hold dollars, and foreigners were also buying Indian debt.\par \par \uc2 "Nine percent yield is good enough yield and that, too, with this level of dollar/rupee," he said.\par \par \uc2 But most analysts remain bearish on the rupee, one of Asia's worst performers with a drop of 8 percent versus the dollar this year, just behind the Korean won's fall of nearly 10 percent.\par \par \uc2 "Given India's increasing current account deficit, high dependence on oil imports and inflationary concerns, we expect the rupee to continue to weaken," analysts at \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  said in a note.\par \par \uc2 Goldman expects it to fall to 43.9 per dollar, then 44.1 before rebounding to 42.2 in three, six and 12 months' time respectively.\par \par \uc2 WAIT AND SEE\par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> gained a fifth of a percent to 30.377 per U.S. dollar ahead of a policy review by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is expected to raise interest rates on Thursday by another 12.5 basis points at least to tackle inflation.\par \par \uc2 The Chinese yuan <CNY=CFXS> inched up to a post-revaluation high of 6.8655 per dollar, but it was less than a tenth of a percent stronger than Tuesday's close at 6.8699.\par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> was shackled between 1.3672 and 1.3690 per U.S. dollar, while the Malaysian ringgit <MYR=> traded within a narrow range of 3.2535 and 3.2660 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The market seems in a wait-and-see mode ahead of the FOMC decision," said Christy Tan, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Bank of America\uc2 , referring to the Fed's policy committee.\par \par \uc2 The Fed is widely expected to hold interest rates steady but investors will scrutinise the statement accompanying its decision for clues on the future course of monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 It is facing a dilemma, since increasing borrowing costs to quell inflation would put a further brake on the weak economy.\par \par \uc2 The Thai baht <THB=TH> fell to a six-month low of 33.60 per dollar as political tensions weighed on the unit.\par \par \uc2 Thai Prime Minister Samak Sundaravej's office remains under siege from hundreds of protesters and the opposition has launched a no-confidence motion against his five-month-old coalition, although the move is largely symbolic. [ID:nBKK149866].\par \par \uc2 "Notwithstanding, persisting tensions among policy makers and the distractions from economic policy will likely persist as a near-term drag on the baht," \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  analysts said. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0758 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 