\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korean won falls on Fed, foreigners stock deals\b0\par\par\uc2 502 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2008\par 02:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)\par \par \uc2 SEOUL, June 11 (Reuters) - The South Korean won slid against the dollar on Wednesday as foreign investors continued to sell domestic shares and following comments from U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke on inflation.\par \par \uc2 Investors remained cautious over possible dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check inflation, but the authorities were not spotted of selling the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The local unit is expected to remain under pressure as fears of inflation are likely to prevent investors from buying riskier assets although the government will step in to curb its sharp falls, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "Globally, all investors are concerned over inflation amid weak economic growth and their appetite for riskier assets is getting weaker," said Lee Tark-koo, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at KB Futures Co Ltd.\par \par \uc2 "The won may rebound a bit when the authorities take measures, but its falling trend is intact," he added.\par \par \uc2 The won <KRW=> was quoted at 1,029.75/30.25 per dollar as of 0600 GMT, compared to its previous domestic closing bid of 1,025.3.\par \par \uc2 The South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened to as high as 1,022.8, helped by demand from exporters for settlements, which looked like the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Sudden dollar sales caused market players to suspect \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but they were exporter deals," said a foreign bank dealer.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  jumped on suspected government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which came after data showed annual producer price inflation in May hit a near 10-year high led by energy prices.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Kang Man-soo said on Wednesday that the government, faced with slowing domestic demand and high inflation, would focus on stabilising the economy, a local news website reported. [ID:nSEO327566]\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors sold a net 294.1 billion won worth of shares in South Korea's main stock market after dumping a combined 437 billion won during the previous two sessions.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark KOSPI <.KS11> ended up 0.41 percent.\par \par \uc2 Speaking late Monday, Bernanke said the Fed would resist rising inflation expectations and added that the latest surge in energy costs was adding to price pressures, prompting investors to forecast a interest rate hike and a strengthening dollar.\par \par \uc2 Investors are keeping an eye on South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's interest rate setting meeting on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Korea is expected to leave interest rates on hold for the 10th consecutive month, as the authorities see inflation being a far greater threat than an economic slowdown, a Reuters poll showed. [ID:nSEO301186]\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                       0600 GMT       0241 GMT     prev close\par  Won <KRW=>        1,029.75/30.25    1,027.4/7.7      1,025.3/8\par  Yen/won <JPYKRW=R>     9.5590/36      9.5629/03       9.6020/76\par  KOSPI <.KS11>           1,781.67       1,777.82       1,774.38\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Cheon Jong-woo; Editing by Keiron Henderson)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080614e46b0000e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw