\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korean won cuts losses on exporters' demand\b0\par\par\uc2 490 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 April 2008\par 10:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Repeats with no changes to text)\par \par \uc2 Updates to close)\par \par \uc2 SEOUL, April 16 (Reuters) - The South Korean hit a three-week low on Wednesday, but later clawed back its losses as demand from exporters for settlements and big foreign orders made investors cut their dollar holdings.\par \par \uc2 The won initially came under pressure from talk of possible dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities after Finance Minister Kang Man-soo expressed worries about current account deficits.\par \par \uc2 However, rising local stocks and large export orders reported by leading companies, offered the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  support, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "Authorities are a very important factor to watch. However, they cannot run against a trend of the won if the unit rises on improvement in fundamentals," said Lee Tark-koo, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at KB Futures Co Ltd.\par \par \uc2 The won <KRW=> was quoted at 989.3/989.6 per dollar at 0600 GMT after falling as low as 995.4, its weakest since March 28. Its previous closing bid was 986.5.\par \par \uc2 The Finance Minister said there were "speculators" in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and the government needed to take steps in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when problems occurred.\par \par \uc2 A day earlier he voiced official concern about widening current account deficits, spurring speculation that the authorities could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the won and help the country's exporters.\par \par \uc2 But Lee said the current account balance should improve as \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  outflows driven by dividend payments of local companies to foreign shareholders were set to be completed this month and the global credit fears were subsiding.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors sold a net 265.6 billion won worth of shares on the country's main exchange after having dumped 1.42 trillion won during the last four consecutive sessions.\par \par \uc2 But the won drew some support from a 0.94 percent rise in Seoul's benchmark index <.KS11> and bids for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by exporters.\par \par \uc2 Samsung Heavy Industries Co Ltd\uc2  , the world's second-biggest shipbuilder, said it had secured a 451.8 billion won ($457 million) ship order from Europe, spurring expectations for increased won demand. [ID:nSEL000046]\par \par \uc2 South Korea's \uc2 Doosan Heavy Industries\uc2  also said it had clinched a 115 billion won order for cranes from Singapore. [ID:nSEO86752]\par \par \uc2 Separately, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed net dollar/won forward sales by South Korean exporters in the first quarter rose 37.3 percent from the previous quarter, reflecting investor expectations for a rise in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID:nSEL000047]\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                           0600 GMT     0348 GMT   prev close\par   Won <KRW=>                989.3/9.6    991.5/2.3        986.5\par   Yen/won <JPYKRW=R>       9.7286/344   9.7473/581       9.6849\par   KOSPI <.KS11>              1,758.56     1,758.04     1,742.17\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ($1=988.7 Won) (Reporting by Cheon Jong-woo; Editing by Tomasz Janowski)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2, REPEAT)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080419e44g0007o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\