\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-S.Korea sold dollars to calm markets-dealers   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Yoo Choonsik and Cheon Jong-woo   \par \uc2 634 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 01:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Recasts throughout)   \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, March 18 (Reuters) - South Korea sold about $1 billion for won on Tuesday, dealers said, stemming losses of 8.5 percent in the past 12 sessions as the new government strives to keep its economic policy on track ahead of key elections next month.   \par \par \uc2 The won <KRW=> ended local trade up 1 percent against the dollar as dealers detected the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by authorities.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the won's drop against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including even the weakening dollar, was in reaction to its excessive rally in 2004-2006 and would deal an especially serious blow to \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  grappling with already-high inflation.   \par \par \uc2 "In part, the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears aimed at next month's elections because a weakening won definitely pushes up inflation at a time when raw materials prices are already rising," said Kim Jae-eun, an economist at Hana Daetoo Securities.   \par \par \uc2 The falling won and the resultant spike in inflation are not welcome developments for the growth-centred new government, installed only last month, especially as it gears up to consolidate power in parliamentary elections on April 9.   \par \par \uc2 The reported dollar purchases marked the first such major \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at propping up the won since early 2002.   \par \par \uc2 A \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  official at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which can buy or sell dollars on behalf of the government when the won moves sharply, declined to comment on the talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Since touching a decade high against the dollar on Oct. 31, 2007, the won has lost 11 percent against the dollar, 25 percent against the yen <JPYKRW=R>, 18 percent against the euro <EURKRW=R> and 16 percent against the yuan <CNYKRW=R>.   \par \par \uc2 ORDERLY DECLINE   \par \par \uc2 As the falling won is unnerving investors, the Finance Ministry said late on Tuesday that senior officials from the ministry, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other government agencies would meet early on Wednesday to check financial market movements.   \par \par \uc2 Prime Minister Han Seung-soo also told a cabinet meeting on Tuesday to draw up measures to stabilise domestic prices, a government spokesman said.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed on Sunday import prices measured in won terms rose a whopping 22.2 percent in February from a year earlier, the fastest annual gain since October 1998.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts said \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reported \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not seen as a concerted action with other countries, and added it appeared aimed at smoothing the won's decline rather than turning the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  around.   \par \par \uc2 "I think they do not want a disorderly decline like yesterday's 3 percent move," said Tim Condon, head of Asia research at investment bank ING, referring to the won's 3.3 percent peak-to-peak movement on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 "However, the Korean won was among Asia's top-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2004-2006 and I am beginning to think the authorities would like to see it retrace the gains of those years, which would put it above 1,100 against the U.S. dollar and above 11 against the Japanese yen."   \par \par \uc2 The won's value against the yen -- quoted based on each \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's movements against the dollar -- has fallen to 10.42 from 7.80 on Oct. 31, 2007.   \par \par \uc2 Research company IDEAglobal's index measuring the won's value against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  <KRWNEERI=IDEA> shows the won has outperformed its rivals since late 2004 until recently.   \par \par \uc2 A weaker won helps exporters by making their products cheaper in dollar terms or improving their profit margins, but the effect could easily be negated by the shrinking demand for goods from around the world in the face of a global slowdown. (Editing by Keiron Henderson)   \par \par \uc2 KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080321e43i00004\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
