\par\par \b \uc2 Bank Of Korea Official: Recent USD/KRW Rise "Too Sharp"   \b0\par\par\uc2 269 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 01:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SEOUL (Dow Jones)--A senior Bank of Korea official said Tuesday that the dollar's recent surge against the won seems "too sharp," and that the country's current account is likely to remain in a deficit until April, indicating that the dollar might continue to rise in the weeks ahead.   \par \par \uc2 Ahn Byung-Chan, director-general of the Bank of Korea's international department, said that the dollar's gains will likely persist in the first half, but that trend could reverse in the second half of the year.   \par \par \uc2 He also said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is watching the market closely, suggesting that it could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by selling the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Late last month, Kang Man-Soo, speaking at a National Assembly committee hearing prior to his appointment as finance minister, said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deemed that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves of $250 billion are adequate, based on the country's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt and foreigners' holding of local shares.   \par \par \uc2 His statement suggested that the Bank of Korea has the means to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market by unloading dollars.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves totaled $262.36 billion at the end of February.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar opened sharply higher against the won Tuesday, hitting a two-year intraday high of KRW974.51 at 0023 GMT.That was its highest level since March 31, 2006, when it had risen to an intraday high of KRW977.04.   \par \par \uc2 -By Jung-Ah Lee, Dow Jones Newswires; 822-732-2165;jung-ah.lee@dowjones.com [ 11-03-08 0027GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080311e43b0000c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
