\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea won falls on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  after 10-yr high   \b0\par\par\uc2 474 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Oktober 2007\par 01:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Oct 30 (Reuters) - The South Korean won <KRW=> edged down against the dollar on Tuesday as the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities were suspected of buying dollars after the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a fresh decade high.   \par \par \uc2 South Korea also warned it would take measures to smooth the won's rise if the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate was "distorted excessively".   \par \par \uc2 The won was last quoted at 906.8/7.4 per dollar, after rising to as high as 904.1, its strongest since Sept. 4, 1997. That compared to its previous closing bid of 906.4.   \par \par \uc2 "The authorities bought a massive amount of dollars to push down the won just before the market closed. That totally overturned market sentiment for a higher won," said a local bank dealer. He declined to comment on the specific amount.   \par \par \uc2 On Monday, \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities were suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight in the overseas dollar/won non-deliverable forwards (NDF) market after being spotted buying dollars in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 Still, dealers expect the won to rise further on expectations for interest rate cuts by the U.S. Federal Reserve and helped by demand from exporters for end-month settlements.   \par \par \uc2 A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official's optimistic view of the current account and other data demonstrating strength in Asia's fourth-largest economy are also likely to provide support to the won.   \par \par \uc2 Jeong Sam-young, head of the Bank of Korea's international balance of payments team, told reporters that South Korea was expected to exceed the $2 billion surplus forecast for 2007, despite a 40 percent fall in a seasonally adjusted current account surplus last month. [ID:nSEO194379]   \par \par \uc2 South Korea's industrial output fell a seasonally adjusted 0.1 percent in September from August, separate data showed, compared with an expected 1.0 percent fall in a Reuters poll. [ID:nSEW000202]   \par \par \uc2 The dollar slightly rebounded from record lows against the euro and a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but remained under pressure by expectations the Fed will cut interest rates to keep the world's top economy from a severe slowdown.   \par \par \uc2 The yen <JPY=> was at 114.40/43 per dollar versus 114.61/65 in late New York trade on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 Seoul shares <.KS11> ended down 0.51 percent with foreign investors buying a net 86.9 billion won worth of shares in the country's main stock market.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                        0720 GMT     0310 GMT   prev close\par  Won <KRW=>              906.8/7.4    907.6/8.2        906.4\par  Yen/won <JPYKRW=R>     7.9252/318   7.9253/319       7.9010\par  KOSPI <.KS11>            2,052.37     2,054.67     2,062.92\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071102e3au0001i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
