\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korean won gains on record stocks, Fed minutes   \b0\par\par\uc2 383 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 2007\par 03:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2   (Updates to midday)   \par \par \uc2  SEOUL, Oct 10 (Reuters) - The South Korean won <KRW=> gained against the dollar on Wednesday as Seoul shares hit yet another record and after the Federal Reserve's minutes indicated the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may cut interest rates further if necessary.   \par \par \uc2  But rises in the won were capped as importers sold the unit for settlements and on lingering concerns over possible dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities.   \par \par \uc2  The won was quoted at 916.0/6.7 per dollar by 0325 GMT, compared to its previous closing bid of 918.1.   \par \par \uc2  "Investors are chasing the won in line with overall gains in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The won's falls yesterday were just a correction," said a foreign bank dealer.   \par \par \uc2  The dollar remained weak after Fed minutes on Tuesday showed that all of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's board members had agreed to cut federal funds rate by 50 basis points to 4.75 percent last month on concerns that a credit crunch and the resulting market turmoil might harm the U.S. economy.   \par \par \uc2  Seoul shares <.KS11> rose 1.18 percent, after hitting a record high of 2,044.78, its third in three days, with foreign investors selling a net 39.4 billion won worth of shares in the country's main stock market.   \par \par \uc2  On the corporate front, SK Energy Co 's chairman Chey Tae-won said on Tuesday the South Korea's top oil refiner was interested in investing up to $2 billion in a sprawling petrochemicals complex in Peru, raising expectations of won supplies. [ID:nN09431218]   \par \par \uc2  Korea Electric Power Corp (KEPCO)  also said on Tuesday it planned to invest up to $1.43 billion in buying stakes in power generators in China and Russia. [ID:nSEO236736]   \par \par \uc2  The yen <JPY=> was at 117.16/20 per dollar versus 117.12/14 in late New York trade on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                       0325 GMT      0115 GMT    prev close\par  Won <KRW=>             916.0/6.5     915.9/6.5         918.1\par  Yen/won <JPYKRW=R>    7.8170/228     7.8154/86        7.8370\par  KOSPI <.KS11>           2,037.97      2,039.00      2,014.13\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071013e3aa00015\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
