\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea BOK says may step in again in swaps market   \b0\par\par\uc2 262 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2007\par 02:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Sept 12 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in the local dollar/won swaps market if it is necessary to stabilise the market, a senior official at the Bank of Korea (BOK) told Reuters on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 Ahn Byung-chan, director of international department, also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on Tuesday because a prolonged short supply of dollars.   \par \par \uc2 "I hope the market will return to normal gradually, but we will take action if any such supply-demand imbalance takes place in the future," he said.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders estimated the Bank of Korea had injected about $500 million into the market through the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, but Ahn declined to disclose the size or nature of its market manoeuvres.   \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Korea banned last month commercial banks from providing foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans whose proceeds are eventually to be converted into the won <KRW=> and are not for settlements on purchases of production equipment.   \par \par \uc2 Banks have complained the measure, aimed at preventing the won from strengthening against the dollar, has sparked a severe shortage of dollars on the swaps market, in the process pushing up the costs of hedging for export companies.   \par \par \uc2 Exporters and institutional investors in overseas markets hedge against the risks from future \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  changes by selling dollar/won forwards to banks, which in turn borrow dollars or swap the won for the dollar to take up the deals.   \par \par \uc2 KOREA-ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|ABX|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070912e39c00011\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
