\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea won gains on easing credit market worries   \b0\par\par\uc2 552 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 2007\par 02:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Update to close)   \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, July 31 (Reuters) - The South Korean won <KRW=> rose against the dollar on Tuesday as abating worries about credit markets revived appetite for the local unit, which also gained on exporters' demand for end-month settlements.   \par \par \uc2 Market players also cleared dollar-long positions they had built on concerns over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and avoidance of risky assets.   \par \par \uc2 The won is expected to strengthen further as investors resume their preference for emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the won and as exporters continue to seek the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "The won will maintain its rising trend on improvements in economic fundamentals and as the unit's gain lagged other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a local bank dealer.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will eventually test its highs as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and regulations probably won't stop the won's rise but merely slow its pace," he added.   \par \par \uc2 But the local unit gave up some of its gains as investors stayed wary of South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities' plans to check the won's rise and as foreign investors continued to sell Seoul shares.   \par \par \uc2 The won was last quoted at 919.2/9.4 per dollar, compared to its previous closing bid of 923.   \par \par \uc2 Concerns about problems in the U.S. subprime mortgage market spreading to wider credit markets had prompted investors to cut risk exposure.   \par \par \uc2 But higher U.S. stocks overnight eased fears about deteriorating credit markets, helping halt risk aversion that had led to the unwinding of carry trades.   \par \par \uc2 The yen was at 119.0/9.4 per dollar versus 119.14/17 in late New York trade on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 However, global credit risks are expected to continue to put pressure on the won in August, although the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to find some support from exporters, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 The won is seen trading between 914.5 per dollar and 931 next month, according to a Reuters poll.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers kept an eye out for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sources said \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might announce next week measures to restrict the way foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  borrowings are used. [ID:nSEO25667]   \par \par \uc2 Foreign investors sold a net 128.8 billion won worth of shares in Seoul's main stock market, after dumping a combined net 4.78 trillion won in shares during the prior 11 sessions.   \par \par \uc2 But the benchmark KOSPI <.KS11> ended up 1.39 percent.   \par \par \uc2 On the economic front, overseas direct investments by South Koreans rose 44 percent to $10.3 billion in the first half from a year ago, Finance Ministry data showed.   \par \par \uc2 Investors are looking to economic data on Wednesday, including July's exports.   \par \par \uc2 South Korea's annual export growth probably hit a six-month high in July, a Reuters poll showed, supporting hopes for a faster economic recovery. [ID:nSEO269310]   \par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, data showed service sector output in Asia's fourth-largest economy rose a seasonally adjusted 1.1 percent in June over a month earlier. [ID:nSEV000123]   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                     0720 GMT     0442 GMT   prev close\par  Won <KRW