\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea won up on abated risk aversion, exporters   \b0\par\par\uc2 352 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 2007\par 02:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Update to midday)   \par \par \uc2  SEOUL, July 31 (Reuters) - The South Korean won gained against the dollar on Tuesday as eased concerns about credit markets prompted appetite for the local unit, which was also helped by demand from exporters for end-month settlements.   \par \par \uc2  Market players also cleared dollar-long positions they had built due to wariness of dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and an avoidance of risky assets.   \par \par \uc2  But the won's gains were capped as dealers remained concerned over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities and as foreign investors kept selling Seoul shares.   \par \par \uc2  The won <KRW=> was quoted at 919.2/7 per dollar by 0442 GMT, compared to its previous closing bid of 923.   \par \par \uc2  "The won may rise further despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears as aversion to risks abated, prompting investors to buy the unit," said a foreign bank dealer.   \par \par \uc2  Concerns about problems in the U.S. subprime mortgage market spreading to wider credit markets had prompted investors to cut risk exposure.   \par \par \uc2  The yen was at 118.93/96 per dollar versus 119.14/17 in late New York trade on Monday.   \par \par \uc2  The yen has been under pressure as higher U.S. stocks eased fears about deteriorating credit markets, helping to halt risk aversion that had led to the unwinding of carry trades.   \par \par \uc2  But dealers kept an eye out for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sources said \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might announce measures to restrict the way foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  borrowings are used.   \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors sold a net 73.4 billion won worth of shares in Seoul's main stock market, after dumping a combined net 4.78 trillion won in shares during the prior 11 sessions.   \par \par \uc2  However, the benchmark KOSPI <.KS11> rose 0.94 percent.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                     0442 GMT     0015 GMT   prev close\par  Won <KRW=>             919.2/7    920.9/1.4          923\par  Yen/won <JPYKRW=R>  7.7270/340   7.7387/440       7.7511\par  KOSPI <.KS11>         1,924.69     1,908.22     1,906.71\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070803e37v0000t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
