\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea won hits 7-month high on overseas orders   \b0\par\par\uc2 494 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juli 2007\par 02:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to midday)   \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, July 24 (Reuters) - The South Korean won <KRW=> hit a fresh seven-month high against the dollar on Tuesday as domestic companies won big foreign orders and on worries about a fallout from the U.S. housing sector.   \par \par \uc2 But the won failed to extend gains on lingering concerns over possible dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities and as Seoul shares turned lower amid foreigners' sales.   \par \par \uc2 The won was quoted at 914.1/4.6 per dollar by 0315 GMT, compared to its previous closing bid of 914.9. It hit a session high of 913.6, its strongest since 912.6 on Dec. 7, 2006.   \par \par \uc2 "The unit is well supported as most market players opt to buy the won on any dips," said a foreign bank dealer.   \par \par \uc2 "The won is likely to maintain its strength if we do not see actions from the authorities, but they do not seem to be inclined to push down the won," he added.   \par \par \uc2 Adding to expectations for won demand, South Korea's Daewoo Shipbuilding and Marine Engineering Co. said it had won a 578.9 billion won order to build a semi-submersible production and drilling facility for an unidentified company in the Americas. [ID:nSEL000045]   \par \par \uc2 The shipbuilder said it has secured a combined $13 billion in orders, with $4 billion in July, so far this year, out of its 2007 order target of $17 billion.   \par \par \uc2 Also, Samsung Engineering & Construction Co. said it had won a $470 million order to build a plant in Thailand. [ID:nSEL000047]   \par \par \uc2 But a major foreign investment plan by South Korean companies prompted investors to expect won supplies.   \par \par \uc2 South Korea's Kenertec Co. said it would finalise a $5.5 billion direct coal liquefaction project in Indonesia with PT Nuansa Cipta Coal Investment and  \uc2 POSCO\uc2  Engineering and Construction, a unit of POSCO Co. Ltd. . [ID:nSEO223212]   \par \par \uc2 Also, South Koreans' foreign property purchases jumped 86 percent in the first half from a year ago after the country eased rules on overseas property investment, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed on Tuesday. [ID:nSEO212555]   \par \par \uc2 In Seoul's main stock market, foreign investors sold a net 91.2 billion won worth of shares after dumping a combined net 2.13 trillion won in the previous six sessions.   \par \par \uc2 The benchmark KOSPI <.KS11> fell 0.63 percent after breaking above the 2,000-point level for the first time earlier.   \par \par \uc2 The yen <JPY=> was at 120.53/54 versus per dollar versus 120.98/01 in late New York trade on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                      0315 GMT     0020 GMT   prev close\par  Won <KRW=>            914.1/4.6    914.3/5.0        914.9\par  Yen/won <JPYKRW=R>    7.5800/56    7.5700/70       7.5562\par  KOSPI <.KS11>          1,980.42     1,995.43     1,993.05\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2   (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070727e37o00062\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
