\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-S.Korea producer inflation boosts rate rise bets   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Lee Jin-joo and Yoo Choonsik   \par \uc2 569 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juli 2007\par 05:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds analyst, background)   \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, July 9 (Reuters) - South Korea's producer inflation in June hit a nine-month high, data showed on Monday, giving fresh ammunition to a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that is already seen poised to raise interest rates for the first time in almost a year.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the producer price index in June rose 2.7 percent from a year earlier, the fastest since a 3.1 percent gain in September last year, led by accelerating growth in service prices such as utility fees.   \par \par \uc2 The data comes just a day after figures showing the country's money supply growth picked up in May and the government's upgrade of its 2007 export forecast provided more incentive for the Bank of Korea to lift interest rates at its July 12 policy meeting. [ID:nSEO44783] [ID:nSEO359896]   \par \par \uc2 "Annual producer prices have risen, giving support to increasing expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will raise interest rates in July amid faster growth in the domestic economy," said Lee Sang-jae, an economist at  \uc2 Hyundai Securities.\par \par \uc2 Echoing such expectations, a majority of bond dealers said in an industry survey on Monday that the Bank of Korea would raise the overnight call rate target on Thursday, after having held it steady at 4.50 percent for 10 months. [ID:nSEO20591]   \par \par \uc2 Investors have already priced in an interest rate increase after Bank of Korea Governor Lee Seong-tae warned in early June high liquidity could stoke inflation and later said that interest rates were not so high as to hurt economic growth.   \par \par \uc2 Figures released last week also underscored that Asia's fourth-largest economy was gathering steam, with the June trade surplus hitting an all-time high on brisk exports and that month's consumer inflation picking up. [ID:nSEO355036]   \par \par \uc2 ROOM FOR WON'S RISE   \par \par \uc2 Analysts expect higher local interest rates and resilient export demand for South Korean products to create room for the won <KRW=> to gain further after having risen 25 percent against the U.S. dollar over the past three years.   \par \par \uc2 "There is a strong possiblity that the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may rise after the Bank of Korea tightens its monetary policy, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has other means to keep the won down, by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," Lee said.   \par \par \uc2 The government-run  \uc2 Korea Development Bank\uc2  forecast on Monday the won would rise to an average of 915 per dollar for the second half of this year from 933.6 for the first half. The won was quoted at 920.1 by 0421 GMT, down 0.11 percent.   \par \par \uc2 South Korean policy makers have expressed concern that the won's appreciation against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was hurting export companies by making their products more expensive in dollar terms and eroding exporters' profits in won terms.   \par \par \uc2 But analysts say \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as actively as they did in 2003-2004, due to increased pressure over billions of dollars in losses incurred from the prior \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 They said strong exports despite the won's rise also left the Finance Ministry and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  with little excuse to dump the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could risk pushing up already-buoyant local liquidity growth.   \par \par \uc2 KOREA-ECONOMY/PPI (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070709e3790003y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
