\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-S.Korea  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves fall in June on swap deals   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Cheon Jong-woo and Yoo Choonsik   \par \uc2 509 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 2007\par 23:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Recasts with details, background)   \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, July 3 (Reuters) - South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell in June for the first time in a year as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expanded \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps as a way to cheaply soak up liquidity, the Bank of Korea said on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , under mounting pressure to cut the costs of draining surplus liquidity through bonds, said it swapped about $660 million in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the won with the state-run pension agency and local banks in June.   \par \par \uc2 The amount was more than the usual $500 million swapped in the past, an official at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.   \par \par \uc2 It was also greater than the capital gains from investments of the reserves funds, resulting in a decline in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves by $40 million from a month before, to $250.70 billion at end-June, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.   \par \par \uc2 It was the first time that the country's foreign reserves, which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  manages, recorded a monthly decline since dropping by $332 million in June 2006.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been struggling to contain the costs of skimming off growing won liquidity, which it undertakes to keep inflationary pressures in check.   \par \par \uc2 It posted a net loss of 1.76 trillion won ($1.91 billion) in 2006 after losing 1.88 trillion won in 2005, mainly because it paid more than 6 trillion won in each year in interest on monetary stabilisation bonds (MSBs), \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data shows.   \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Korea has pledged on several occasions to seek alternative ways to absorb liquidity and had actually sharply cut net new issuances of MSBs offered in 2006, according to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data posted on its Web site (  {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bok.or.kr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.bok.or.kr  }}}\uc2 ).   \par \par \uc2 The outstanding amount of MSBs issued grew only 2 percent by the end of 2006 from a year before after rises of 9 percent in 2005 and 35 percent in 2004.   \par \par \uc2 Swapping some of the reserves held in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the won held by the National Pension Service, which manages more than $200 billion, helps the Bank of Korea absorb the extra won in the financial system without selling bonds.   \par \par \uc2 South Korea has been enjoying a net capital inflow for years due to trade surpluses and foreign investment, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought much of the surplus dollars on the market to keep the won <KRW=> from appreciating quickly.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government has said such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was inevitable to protect exporters, important contributors to the growth of Asia's fourth-largest economy, from the won's rises. A strong local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  can hurt exporters' profitability and competitiveness.   \par \par \uc2 But despite several years of dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the won has continued to gain against the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and was not far from its strongest mark in nearly a decade against the dollar on Tuesday afternoon.   \par \par \uc2 KOREA-ECONOMY/RESERVES (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|ABX|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070702e372001yn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
