\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 South Korea \highlight\uc2  won firmer,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  talk lingers   \b0\par\par\uc2 367 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 2007\par 02:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to midday)   \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, June 20 (Reuters) - The South Korean won rose against the dollar on Wednesday after a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said the Bank of Korea was limited in influencing exchange rates, but caution over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  capped the won's gains.   \par \par \uc2 The won <KRW=> was quoted at 925.5/6.2 per dollar at 0325 GMT, up from Tuesday's close at 927.4/8.0, after hitting a session high bid of 924.6, the strongest since May 17.   \par \par \uc2 It also rose against the Japanese yen <JPYKRW=R> to hit a nine-and-a-half-year high bid of 7.4897, before retreating slightly to 7.5024/105.   \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Kwon O-kyu said on Wednesday authorities would carry out "smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 " if speculative trading moves the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.   \par \par \uc2 "Trading is stalled as there is lots of caution but no actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a dealer at a foreign bank.   \par \par \uc2 South Korean authorities usually buy dollars for the won to stem the local unit's strength, which hurts export performance.   \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Korea's senior deputy governor, Lee Sung-il, told Reuters late on Tuesday in Chatham, Massachusetts, that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was concerned about the won's strength, especially against the Japanese unit.   \par \par \uc2 But he acknowledge it could do little about it.   \par \par \uc2 "As you know, the yen/won rate is decided by arbitrage of the yen/dollar rate so we don't have a choice," he said on the sidelines of a conference. Asked if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would take action to restrain the won's rise, he said: "No." [ID:nN19188694]   \par \par \uc2 The Seoul stock market's benchmark KOSPI <.KS11> was down 0.31 percent, with foreign investors selling a net 278.5 billion won worth of shares on the main board.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                        0325 GMT     0040 GMT   prev close\par  Won <KRW=>              925.5/6.2    925.5/6.2    927.4/8.0\par  Yen/won <JPYKRW=R>     7.5024/105    7.5006/81    7.5160/27\par  KOSPI <.KS11>            1,802.17     1,806.04     1,807.85\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070623e36k0000i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
