\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 South Korea \highlight\uc2  renews  \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention \highlight\uc2  pledge   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Yoo Choonsik   \par \uc2 531 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 2007\par 04:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Recasts throughout with officials, OECD)   \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, June 20 (Reuters) - South Korea renewed its pledge on Wednesday to stem the won's rise, dismissing suggestions that criticism over losses from past \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was blocking the government from stepping in now to tame the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The authorities have both the ability and the will to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when necessary to cap the won's <KRW=> appreciation against the U.S. dollar, Deputy Finance Minister Kim Sung-jin told a private seminar.   \par \par \uc2 His comments, which came hours after similar warnings by Finance Minister Kwon O-kyu, were in contrast to an Organisation for Economic Co-\b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Development (OECD) call for more tolerance of the won's appreciation.   \par \par \uc2 "Some say the hands of the government and the Bank of Korea remain tied because of losses incurred from past \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it's completely wrong," said Kim, the highest official after the minister and vice minister to decide on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The Paris-based OECD pressed \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Asia's fourth-largest economy, to be flexible over the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "Maintaining a flexible exchange rate policy will help boost domestic demand, while export growth appears increasingly resilient to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  changes," the agency said in a report.   \par \par \uc2 South Korean policy makers are worried about the won's steep appreciation over the past few years, not only against the dollar but also compared to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of chief export rivals Japan and China.   \par \par \uc2 The won has gained only 0.2 percent against the dollar this year but has jumped about 4 percent against the yen <JPYKRW=R>, hitting a 9-1/2-year high on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 NO INFLATION WORRY   \par \par \uc2 Both South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the OECD sounded upbeat on the economic growth and inflation outlook for 2007-2008.   \par \par \uc2 "The economy is expected to gradually reverse the slowdown experienced during (the latter part of) 2006, with growth of around 4-\u188\'00\'BC percent in 2007, despite the tightening of monetary conditions," the OECD said.   \par \par \uc2 South Korea's economy grew by 5.0 percent in 2006 after 4.2 percent in 2005.   \par \par \uc2 The OECD forecast gross domestic product growth would rise further to 4-\u190\'00\'BE percent in 2008.   \par \par \uc2 The economy looks relatively free of any immediate risk from inflation, both the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the OECD said.   \par \par \uc2 "We don't much worry about this year's price growth," Lee Ju-yeol, a deputy governor at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , told the same seminar for financial market experts.   \par \par \uc2 "It's true to some extent that inflation pressure is growing along with rising inflation in China, but, overall, that will not likely pose a serious threat through next year," he said.   \par \par \uc2 The OECD also noted the tame inflation in South Korea, advising the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to focus its monetary policy on the stable inflation trend rather than use it as a tool to cool the booming housing market.   \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Korea has held interest rates steady for 10 successive months after lifting them by a combined 1.25 percentage points on five occasions until August 2006.   \par \par \uc2 KOREA-ECONOMY/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070620e36k0003t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
