\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea May  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves soar as  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  spotted   \b0\par\par\uc2 286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juni 2007\par 23:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  SEOUL, June 4 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose the most in five months in May, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed on Monday, as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers and analysts suspected that the country bought dollars to check the won's <KRW=> strength.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  The country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves -- the world's\par fifth-largest in April -- rose to $250.7 billion as of the end of\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 May from $247.3 billion a month ago, the Bank of Korea said in a statement.   \par \par \uc2  The gain of $3.48 billion , or 1.4 percent, was the largest since a $4.7 billion rise posted in December 2006.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market players have said huge changes in foreign reserves usually reflect the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.   \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Korea attributed the rise in May to investment gains.   \par \par \uc2  But dealers and analysts in Seoul said the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities had been suspected of buying about a combined $2.5 billion during the month.   \par \par \uc2  Officials at the finance ministry and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment.   \par \par \uc2  South Korean foreign reserves have risen by 4.9 percent, or $11.78 billion, so far this year, Bank of Korea data shows. Its reserves rank behind those of China, Japan, Russia and Taiwan.   \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said 88.2 percent of April's total reserves were invested in securities, compared with 11.6 percent deposited at financial institutions.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   South Korea's foreign reserves ($ billion, at end-month):\par  May       April    March    February   January  December\par  250.74    247.26   243.92   242.81     240.23   238.96\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 KOREA-ECONOMY/RESERVES|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|ABX|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070603e363000km\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
