\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-S.Korea suspected of  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  for 2nd day   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Cheon Jong-woo   \par \uc2 444 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 2007\par 06:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official's comment in paras 8-9)   \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, May 18 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities were suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily on Friday to sell the won for the dollar, pushing it to a six-week low and underlining their determination to prevent the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from rising further.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said they believed authorities had bought $1 billion for the second day in a row. On Thursday, the won hit its highest level in almost a decade against the yen and it was gaining against the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 "Investors will not dare to build up dollar-short positions for the rest of this year after the government took extremely strong action," said a foreign bank dealer.   \par \par \uc2 Dollar spot trading volume hit a record high of $12.49 billion on Friday, the Seoul Money Brokerage Services Ltd. and  \uc2 Korea Money Broker Corp.\uc2  said.   \par \par \uc2 That was almost twice the daily average volume in 2007 of $6.9 billion.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has helped knock the won down more than 1.2 percent over two days against the dollar and by 0.8 percent against the yen <JPYKRW=R>.   \par \par \uc2 The won fell to an intraday low of 935.1 per dollar on Friday, its lowest value since 936.2 on April 5.   \par \par \uc2 An official at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  told Reuters after the end of the local trading that exporters had sold more than $5 billion over the two days, much higher than normal volume of less than $1 billion on a typical day.   \par \par \uc2 The official, who declined to be named, did not elaborate.   \par \par \uc2 The suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  followed warnings by a deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor on Tuesday that the won was overvalued.   \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Korea and the finance ministry issued a rare joint statement on Thursday saying they were closely watching the won's movements and will take action if necessary.   \par \par \uc2 The won has risen about 30 percent against the dollar in 2004-2006, but is one of the poorest performers in Asia so far this year.   \par \par \uc2 However, South Korean policy makers have complained the past gains were already excessive when compared to rival \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 They say they are concerned with the won's strength not just against the U.S. dollar but against Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well.   \par \par \uc2 A rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  can make South Korean exports more expensive compared with those of regional competitors and can undermine exporters' profitability when they repatriate overseas earnings. (Additional reporting by Kim Yeon-hee and Lee Soo-jung)   \par \par \uc2 KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|ABX|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070521e35i00097\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
