\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 South Korea \highlight\uc2  suspected of $1 bln  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Cheon Jong-woo   \par \uc2 511 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2007\par 06:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Adds amount of suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , economist comment)   \par \par \uc2  SEOUL, May 17 (Reuters) - South Korean authorities were cited as having \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  strongly to cap a surging won on Thursday and they sent markets a stark warning that they would do whatever was needed to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength.   \par \par \uc2  Dealers suspected authorities bought up to $1 billion in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market after the won <KRW=> hit its highest level against the yen in almost a decade and as it gained on the dollar.   \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended the day down 0.5 percent against the dollar -- its biggest daily percentage drop in 10 weeks -- and it also backed off the highs against the yen <JPYKRW=R>.   \par \par \uc2  "We saw sudden dollar bid inflows, which were suspected to be from the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so it is becoming more difficult to buy the won from this level," said a foreign bank dealer.   \par \par \uc2  In a rare joint warning, the Bank of Korea and the finance ministry said they were closely watching the won's movements and will take action if necessary.   \par \par \uc2  "The won's recent gains do not reflect economic fundamentals and supply/demand conditions," said Kim Yun-chul, head of the Bank of Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market team.   \par \par \uc2  Moon Hongsung, director of the finance ministry's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market division, made similar comments.   \par \par \uc2  But officials from the Bank of Korea declined to comment on whether authorities had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.   \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the won to stay under pressure from wariness of further dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But it's downside may also be limited in the absence of further action by authorities.   \par \par \uc2  "The government will have to push down the won to 935 with additional strong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  tomorrow; otherwise, exporters and offshore players will chase the won on dips," said another foreign bank dealer, who asked not to be identified.   \par \par \uc2  Offshore players, who heavily influence the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, bought much of the won during the session, he said.   \par \par \uc2  South Korean policy makers say they are concerned with the won's rise not just against the U.S. dollar but against Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well.   \par \par \uc2  A rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  can make South Korean exports more expensive compared with those of regional competitors and can undermine exporters' profitability when they repatriate overseas earnings.   \par \par \uc2  The chief economist at the Samsung Economic Research Institute said the won was overvalued.   \par \par \uc2  "We have done calculations recently based on 1993, when the country's current account was in balance, and it shows the won is 15 percent overvalued now," said Hong Sun-young, director of the economic research department at the institute.   \par \par \uc2  Earlier in the week, a senior Bank of Korea official told Reuters the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was concerned that the won was overvalued and ran the risk of a sharp correction this year. [ID:nSP54563]  (Additional reporting by Yoo Choonsik and Lee Kyoung-ho)      \par \par \uc2 KOREA-ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|ABX|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070520e35h0006g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
