\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Firm tone in Asia, rupiah at 2-1/2-mth high   \b0\par\par\uc2 837 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Mai 2007\par 05:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, May 3 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah hit its highest level in 2-\u189\'00\'BD months against the dollar on Thursday as investors snapped up local assets, while rising regional stock markets boosted other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The high-yielding rupiah <IDR=> rose as high as 9,038 per dollar, up about 0.4 percent from late Asia trade on Wednesday and its highest level since mid-February, as foreign investors bid to buy into the country's stock markets.   \par \par \uc2 "The rise is mostly driven by offshore buying of local assets, such as stocks," said a dealer in Jakarta.   \par \par \uc2 The South Korean won <KRW=> rose to 926.4 per dollar, its highest in a week, as exporters sold dollars. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had weakened in early trade amid caution over \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves swelled by about $3.3 billion in April, the fastest in four months, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed on Thursday, which dealers said reflected increased \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the won's strength.   \par \par \uc2 Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were firm against the dollar, shrugging of yen <JPY=> weakness, but trade was slow with markets in China and Japan closed for holidays.   \par \par \uc2 The interest in the rupiah was largely sparked by expectations that the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was nearing the end of a series of rate cuts, while others said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had underperformed the market.   \par \par \uc2 The Philippine peso <PHP=>, another high-yielder, gained nearly a quarter of a percent to about 47.60 per dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Asian stocks rose on Thursday as MSCI's measure of Asia Pacific stocks excluding Japan <.MSCIAPJ> climbed 0.94 percent.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts in general remain bullish about the underlying strength of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , given the region's solid economic fundamentals buoyed by a hefty trade surplus and capital inflows.   \par \par \uc2 "Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength should still be the name of the game and given that we think the opposite for the U.S. dollar what we're seeing is pretty logical," said Magnus Prim, chief Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at SEB.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE DOLLAR   \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> rose to 1.5217 per U.S. dollar, a day after it slipped to 1.5283, its weakest level since mid-March, as overseas banks moved to cover short positions in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "They were buying (the U.S. dollar) in the last few days, so they are just taking some profits," said a dealer in Singapore.   \par \par \uc2 Soma analysts said the near-term upside for the Singapore dollar may be limited by low local interest rates, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the U.S. dollar's gains versus the Japanese yen.   \par \par \uc2 Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS), manages the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within an undisclosed, trade-weighted band. In its semi-annual policy review last month, it stuck with a policy of letting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciate gradually within the band.   \par \par \uc2 Claudio Piron and Yen Ping Ho at  \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  estimated that the Singapore dollar's nominal effective exchange rate (NEER) had slipped into the bottom half of the band for the first time since December 2005.   \par \par \uc2 "The local rates decline was likely the dominant driver. The more cautious read to the MAS statement last month could have contributed in part to this post-statement decline," they said in a research note.   \par \par \uc2 But analysts also saw opportunities to buy into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "As the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stance is still to go for the Singapore dollar's appreciation to curb rising inflation, further weakening of SGD would present a good entry point to enter a Singapore dollar-basket trade," Shiang Hue Lye, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN AMRO, said in a research note. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0759 GMT    \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       120.14         119.91       -0.19\par  Sing dlr        1.5223         1.5271       +0.32\par  Taiwan dlr      33.286         33.286       +0.00\par  Korean won      926.80         929.90       +0.33\par  Baht             34.74          34.76       +0.06\par  Peso             47.51          47.71       +0.42\par  Rupiah         9040.00        9075.00       +0.39\par  Rupee            41.16          41.18       +0.05\par  Ringgit         3.4195         3.4220       +0.07\par  Yuan            7.7039         7.7039       +0.00\par  Change so far in 2007\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       120.14         119.01       -0.94\par  Sing dlr        