\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korean won rises on exporters; 12-wk high vs yen   \b0\par\par\uc2 397 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Mai 2007\par 02:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, May 3 (Reuters) - The South Korean won <KRW=> rose against the dollar on Thursday on exporters' demand and as investors cleared dollar-long positions.   \par \par \uc2 The won also hit a 12-week high versus the yen, which was under pressure on signs that investors continue to borrow the low-yielding Japanese unit to buy higher-yielding assets somewhere else.   \par \par \uc2 But investors were still reluctant to chase the won further as they remained cautious over dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities and amid importers' supplies.   \par \par \uc2 The won was last quoted at 926.7/7.0 per dollar, compared to its previous closing bid of 929.8.   \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  briefly rose to 7.7065 versus the yen, the strongest since reaching 7.6837 on Feb. 13.   \par \par \uc2 "Investors had to square their positions, which they had built on expectations for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as little \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted," said a foreign bank dealer.   \par \par \uc2 "But it is difficult to bet on a further rise in the won because of lingering fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday that banks' increased borrowing of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has negatively affected local financial markets. [ID:nSEO218069]   \par \par \uc2 The country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose the most in four months in April, according to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data, as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market players said the country carried out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID:nSEO217233]   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  expects its exports to slightly slow from May on expectations for a downturn in developed countries and continuing falls in chip prices, a vice finance minister said. [ID:nSEO370093]   \par \par \uc2 The Japanese yen <JPY=> was at 120.09/11 per dollar versus 120.16/20 in late New York on Wednesday. Japanese markets were closed for a holiday on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 Foreign investors sold a net 71.5 billion won in shares on Seoul's main stock market after selling net 17.9 billion won in the previous session.   \par \par \uc2 The benchmark KOSPI <.KS11> closed up 0.42 percent.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                     0640 GMT     0320 GMT   prev close\par  Won <KRW=>           926.7/7.0    929.0/9.8        929.8\par  Yen/won <JPYKRW=R>   7.7154/99   7.7275/348       7.7367\par  KOSPI <.KS11>         1,559.86     1,557.32     1,553.30\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070506e35300009\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
