\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-S.Korea's  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves up as  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  cited   \b0\par\par\uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Mai 2007\par 23:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Recasts with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk, adds background)   \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, May 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose the most in four months in April, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed on Thursday, as \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers and analysts said the country conducted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb strength in the won.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  The country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves -- the world's\par fifth-largest in March -- rose to $247.3 billion as of the end of\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 April from $243.9 billion a month earlier, the Bank of Korea said in a statement.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The gain of $3.3 billion , or 1.4 percent, was the largest since a $4.7 billion rise posted in December. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market players have said big changes in foreign reserves usually reflect the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea attributed the rise in April to strength in non-dollar \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and investment gains.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But dealers and analysts in Seoul said the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities had been suspected of buying about a combined $1 billion during the month.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Officials at the finance ministry and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  declined to comment.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean foreign reserves have risen by 3.5 percent, or $8.3 billion, so far this year, Bank of Korea data shows. Its reserves rank behind those of China, Japan, Russia and Taiwan.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said 85.5 percent of April's total reserves were invested in securities, compared with 14.3 percent deposited at financial institutions.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   South Korea's foreign reserves ($ billion, at end-month):\par  April     March    February   January  December November\par  247.26    243.92   242.81     240.23   238.96   234.26\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 KOREA-ECONOMY/RESERVES (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|ABX|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070502e3520023b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
