\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupee at 9-yr high, won slips on current account   \b0\par\par\uc2 680 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2007\par 05:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, April 26 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee hit a 9-year high on Thursday as investors doubted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's won slipped after data showed the country's current account swung into deficit.   \par \par \uc2 Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were range-bound as the dollar remained within sight of its record low against the euro <EUR=> after mixed U.S. data that did little to allay market fears of a slowdown in the world's largest economy.   \par \par \uc2 "I guess the dollar continues to be in the doldrums with sentiment towards Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  still positive," said Emmanuel Ng, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at  \uc2 OCBC Bank.\par \par \uc2 Suspected dollar-buying by the Bank of Korea also weighed on the won <KRW=>, dealers said, after data showed South Korea's current account swung to a seasonally adjusted deficit of $446 million in March from a surplus in February.   \par \par \uc2 "They don't want the won to go up further as the appreciation may affect the economic picture, but investors, especially foreign investors, still think it's still too cheap," said a dealer at a major Korean bank in Seoul.   \par \par \uc2 The won weakened as low as 930 to the dollar, down almost 0.4 percent from late Asian trade on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 UBS analysts said in a research note that they expected the pace of the won's appreciation against the dollar to slow, but they maintained a three-month forecast of 920 per dollar.   \par \par \uc2 The analysts estimated that the Bank of Korea's average monthly dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had eased to $1.5 billion in the first quarter of this year from $2.0 billion in 2006.   \par \par \uc2 RUPEE SHINES   \par \par \uc2 The Indian rupee <INR=IN> rose as high as 40.71 per dollar as investors shrugged off worries of official steps to limit further gains in Asia's best-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year.   \par \par \uc2 It rallied past 41 on Wednesday for the first time in nine years.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee has risen 8.4 percent against the dollar this year, including an increase of about 3 percent in the past week, which some analysts said could help India check inflationary pressures.   \par \par \uc2 But Reserve Bank of India Governor Yaga Venugopal Reddy said on Wednesday that might not be the case and in fact could fuel demand.   \par \par \uc2 The Philippine peso <PHP=> rose moderately to 47.435 per dollar as concerns over the surprise resignation of the national treasurer eased.   \par \par \uc2 The peso came under brief selling pressure on Wednesday after Omar Cruz quit.   \par \par \uc2 "It's in a tight range but the market seems to have absorbed concerns about Cruz's resignation," a Manila-based trader said.   \par \par \uc2 "They are looking at the possibility that the fiscal position improvements stay intact."   \par \par \uc2 Malaysia's markets were closed on Thursday for a holiday. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0801 GMT    \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       118.94         118.56       -0.32\par  Sing dlr        1.5139         1.5108       -0.20\par  Taiwan dlr      33.216         33.192       -0.07\par  Korean won      928.80         926.60       -0.24\par  Baht             34.79          34.78       -0.03\par  Pe