\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea won steady; exporters seen offseting divs   \b0\par\par\uc2 383 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 2007\par 02:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  0030 GMT - The South Korean won <KRW=> stable against the dollar as exporters' demand for the local unit seen balanced by dividend payments to foreign shareholders.   \par \par \uc2  - A major trade deal between the United States and South Korea received a mixed response on Monday as some U.S. business leaders and politicians complained if fell short on boosting U.S. auto and agricultural exports. [ID:nN02309806]   \par \par \uc2  - Investors prefer bid for the won but also wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities' possible dollar buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rein in strength in the won.   \par \par \uc2  - The dollar fails to give market players momentum to bet in either direction as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  steady on Monday against the yen and the euro on mixed economic data.   \par \par \uc2  - The won quoted at 936.9/7.5 per dollar, compared to its previous closing bid of 936.9.   \par \par \uc2  - "Market players are likely to build up dollar short positions (amid exporter deals) on expectations that the won may rise even to 930 per dollar," says an analyst at a futures firm. "But they are also concerned than the authorities may conduct smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reaches around 935."   \par \par \uc2  - The yen <JPY=> was at 117.82/85 per dollar versus 117.82/86 in late New York trade on Monday.   \par \par \uc2  - On Monday, a survey showed an index of U.S. manufacturing grew at a slower pace in March than in February, with the inflation component showing a jump and emplo