\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 South Korea \highlight\uc2  won tad lower, mild  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  cited  \b0\par\par\uc2 326 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Januar 2007\par 01:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  (Updates to midday)  \par \par \uc2  0335 GMT - The South Korean won <KRW=> a shade lower against the dollar despite a firmer yen <JPY=>, due to what dealers call "smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 " by local authorities to support the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2  - South Korean Finance Minister Kwon O-kyu warned against excessive dollar/won forward sales by local exporters, which the government has blamed for the won's sharp rise against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . See [ID:nSEO66050] for details.  \par \par \uc2  - On top of the suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , offshore investors sell the won for the yen, adding pressure on the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers say.  \par \par \uc2  - Won quoted at 936.7/7.0 per dollar, compared to its previous closing bid of 935.8.  \par \par \uc2  - "It appears that dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  emerged around 935," says a dealer at a foreign bank. "But the dollar is unlikely to gain further due to export settlements."  \par \par \uc2  - The yen quoted at 120.51/53 per dollar, compared to 121.13/16 in late New York trade on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2  - \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market investors shrug off South Korea \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showing the country's economy grew a slower-than-expected 0.8 percent in the fourth quarter of 2006 from the previous quarter. [ID:nSEO14912]  \par \par \uc2  - But some predict a pick-up in Asia's third-largest economy in the second half of this year, potentially prompting further demand for the won.  \par \par \uc2  - On the Seoul stock market, the benchmark stock index KOSPI <.KS11> is up 0.1 percent, with foreign investors buying a net 17.4 billion won worth of shares on the main board.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                      0335 GMT     0030 GMT   prev close\par  Won <KRW=>            936.7/7.0    936.2/6.6        935.8\par  Yen/won <JPYKRW=R>   7.7702/745   7.7399/443       7.7262\par  KOSPI <.KS11>          1,384.40     1,388.45     1,383.06\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070128e31p0000j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
