\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia inches down, shrugging off yen gains  \b0\par\par\uc2 807 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2007\par 03:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Jan 5 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  edged lower on Friday, undermined by a sell-off in commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that overshadowed strong gains in the Japanese yen.  \par \par \uc2 Against the trend, the Philippine peso <PHP=> held near a six-year peak of 48.80 per dollar, supported by upbeat inflation data.  \par \par \uc2 In contrast, the South Korean won <KRW=> fell to a six-week low at about 935 per dollar, the Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> eased 0.3 percent to 32.66 to the U.S. dollar and the Singapore dollar <SGD=> dipped to a session low of 1.5374 per U.S. dollar, within sight of Thursday's one-week trough.  \par \par \uc2 "People are a bit edgy that a pull-back in commodities could mean an adjusting of positions in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well," said Sean Callow, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Westpac Bank.  \par \par \uc2 "We're also coming up to the payrolls report and, if it surprises on the strong side, it could cause a reassessment of the Fed outlook -- so perhaps it's not the best day to be long on risky assets like Asian equities and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 U.S. non-farm payroll figures are due at 1330 GMT. The median forecast in a Reuters poll was for the payrolls to show a gain of 100,000 jobs in December after a 132,000 rise in November.  \par \par \uc2 The Australian and New Zealand dollars <AUD=><NZD=> fell sharply against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , weighed down by softer industrial metals and gains in the yen.  \par \par \uc2 The yen traded at about 118.30 per dollar <JPY=>, up almost 0.9 percent from late Asian trade on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The peso was helped by news that Philippine consumer prices in December rose 4.3 percent from a year earlier, at the lower end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's forecast range, bolstering the prospects of an interest rate cut early this year.  \par \par \uc2 PROBLEMS FOR BAHT, WON  \par \par \uc2 The Thai baht hovered near 36 per dollar <THB=> and was in focus following talk in the market of another coup after the military takeover in September.  \par \par \uc2 Sentiment towards the baht has been hurt in recent weeks, first by the imposition of capital controls and then by bomb attacks that killed three people in Bangkok on New Year's Eve.  \par \par \uc2 "At the moment the talk of a counter-coup in Thailand is being treated as a rumour," said a trader in Hong Kong.  \par \par \uc2 "But the baht is unlikely to follow gains in other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It is a spillover from the New Year bombing and people are afraid of further bad news."  \par \par \uc2 Jitters about Thailand's political situation continued to weigh on the stock market <.SETI>, which was down more than 2 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Sentiment towards the Korean won was undermined by concern about possible government measures to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength.  \par \par \uc2 South Korea's finance minister said late on Thursday the country would not take measures to restrict dollar inflows, a day after the president said he would prevent the won from damaging the economy.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts at UBS said \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  was more likely to step up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to rein in the won than introduce the sort of direct capital controls brought in by the Bank of Thailand in December.  \par \par \uc2 The Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> weakened about a quarter of a percent to 9,020 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "The market is just trying to square up positions," said a dealer in Jakarta. "Liquidity is not too high, so small deals can have a bigger impact." \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0743 GMT   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       118.38         119.31       +0.79\par  Sing dlr        1.5357         1.5336       -0.14\par  Taiwan dlr      32.615         32.550       -0.20\par  Korean won      934.10         931.20       -0.31\par  Baht             35.97          35.95       -0.06\par  Peso             48.81          48.83       +0.04\par  Rupiah         9020.00        8988.00       -0.35\par  Rupee            44.26          44.28       +0.04\par  Ringgit         3.5140         3.5180       +0.11\par  Yuan            7.8078         7.8055       -0.03\par  Change so far in 2007\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       118.38         119.01       +0.53\par  Sing dlr        1.5357         1.5337       -0.13\par  Taiwan dlr      32.615         32.585       -0.09\par  Korean won      934.10        0929.50       -0.49\par  Baht             35.97          36.08       +0.31\par  Peso             48.81          49.03       +0.45\par  Rupiah         9020.00        8988.00       -0.35\par  Rupee            44.26          44.26       -0.02\par  Ringgit         3.5140         3.5270       +0.37\par  Yuan            7.8078         7.8051       -0.03\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|IF|PHD|SI|Z|J|SNS|SNI|ABX|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070108e31500041\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley10