\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 South Korea \highlight\uc2  won steady; wary of  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 401 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 2007\par 02:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Update to close)  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Jan 3 (Reuters) - The South Korean won was virtually unchanged on Wednesday in dull trade, lacking fresh direction with Tokyo financial markets closed for holidays.  \par \par \uc2 Investors remained wary of possible dollar buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by South Korean authorities, while offshore players bought the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but exporters also sold dollars for the won.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier in the day, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves jumped $4.7 billion in December amid dealer reports of heavy government dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at capping the won's rise. [ID:nSEO299509]  \par \par \uc2 The won <KRW=> was last quoted at 925.8/6.3 per dollar, compared to the previous close of 925.3/6.0.  \par \par \uc2 "It is right to sell dollar if the authorities do not show their will," said a local bank dealer.  \par \par \uc2 "The authorities are so sensitive and no one intends to sell the U.S. unit aggressively," he added.  \par \par \uc2 Investors almost ignored South Korea's forecasts for this year's export growth.  \par \par \uc2 Asia's third-largest economy expects export to grow 10.4 percent in 2007, decelerating from a 14.6 percent gain in 2006 hit by a slowdown in the U.S. economy. Imports will probably rise a faster 10.9 percent, resulting in a surplus of $17 billion vs $16.7 billion in 2006. [ID:nSEO143087]  \par \par \uc2 But the won is expected to be supported, given the forecast of a trade surplus, in the longer term although growth in exports is seen slowing, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 The Japanese yen <JPY=> was quoted at 118.81/83 per dollar, compared with 118.85 late in New York, with a holiday in Tokyo keeping trading thin.  \par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the won rose to a nine-year high against the yen as the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains outpaced the yen's.  \par \par \uc2 Seoul's benchmark stock index KOSPI <.KS11> ended down 1.81 percent with foreign investors selling a net 52.2 billion won worth of shares on the main board.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                         0647 GMT      0325 GMT    prev close\par  Won <KRW=>               925.8/6.3       926.1/6     925.3/6.0\par  Yen/won <JPYKRW=R>       7.7916/78   7.7974/8064   7.7854/7933\par  KOSPI <.KS11>             1,409.35      1,427.33      1,435.26\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070106e3130003a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
