\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves jump amid  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  talk  \b0\par\par\uc2 292 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Januar 2007\par 22:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Jan 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves jumped $4.7 billion in December, data showed on Wednesday, amid dealer reports of heavy government dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at capping the won's rise. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, the world's fifth-largest, rose for the sixth consecutive month to $239.0 billion by the end of December from $234.3 billion a month earlier.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Korea attributed the rise to investment gains, receipt of proceeds from the country's sales of about $1 billion in overseas bonds and deposits of required cash reserves from financial institutions.  \par \par \uc2 But the data comes after local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers have suspected the government and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased billions of dollars on the local market in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at capping the won's <KRW=> strength against the dollar and yen.  \par \par \uc2 Traders and analysts are closely looking at the data as any unusual change in the foreign reserves, a majority believed to be invested in dollar assets, could reflect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 Compared with the end of 2005, the country's foreign reserves rose by $28.57 billion, or 13.6 percent, the data showed.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Korea said in the statement the country held 84.5 percent of the total reserves in securities including sovereign bonds and mortgage-backed securities, compared with 15.2 percent held in deposits at financial institutions.  \par \par \uc2 South Korea's foreign reserves ($ billion, at end-month):  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dec      Nov      Oct     Sept      Aug     July\par  238.96   234.26   229.46   228.22   227.02   225.72\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 KOREA-RESERVES/|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070102e31200123\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
