\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea won falls on Thai measures, dlr short-cover  \b0\par\par\uc2 350 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 2006\par 02:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2  SEOUL, Dec 19 (Reuters) - The South Korean won <KRW=> dropped against the dollar for a third session on Tuesday after Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced steps to rein in sharp gains in the baht and amid caution over possible dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2  Some investors kept covering dollar-short positions, putting pressure on the won, although the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut losses due to exporters' dollar supplies.  \par \par \uc2  The won was last quoted at 931.7/2.4 per dollar, compared to the previous closing bid of 926.9.  \par \par \uc2  "Offshore players' dollar purchases were so strong that the won could not defend the level of 930 despite exporters' deals," said a foreign bank dealer.  \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht <THB=> and other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell after Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced on Monday fresh measures to try to curb the baht's rise by forcing speculators to keep their money in the country for at least one year or face stiff financial penalties.  \par \par \uc2  Thai stocks suffered their biggest drop since Asia's 1997 financial crisis as foreign investors were alarmed by the measures, prompting calls for a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  U-turn.  \par \par \uc2  The Japanese yen <JPY=> was quoted at 118.09/12 per dollar versus 118.11/15 in late New York trade.  \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan left interest rates steady at 0.25 percent as widely expected and Governor Toshihiko Fukui said the BOJ does not have a specific schedule in mind in deciding the timing of its next rate rise.  \par \par \uc2  On the Seoul stock market, the benchmark KOSPI <.KS11> ended down 0.38 percent, with foreign investors selling a net 64.1 billion won worth of local shares.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                     0727 GMT    0310 GMT  prev close\par  Won <KRW=>           931.7/2.4   928.6/9.0       926.9\par  Yen/won <JPYKRW=R>  7.8851/930  7.8728/796      7.8458\par  KOSPI <.KS11>         1,427.76    1,432.13    1,433.23\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061222e2cj0001u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
