\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-S.Korea  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves jump as  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  spotted  \b0\par\par\uc2 410 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 2006\par 00:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  (Recasts, adds background)  \par \par \uc2  SEOUL, Dec 4 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose the most in seven months in November, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed on Monday, a month in which dealers said the country carried out heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to contain a rallying won.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  The country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves -- the world's\par fifth-largest in October -- rose for the fifth consecutive month\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to $234.26 billion by the end of November from $229.46 billion a\par month earlier, the Bank of Korea said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  The rise of $4.80 billion, or 2.1 percent, was the largest\par since a $5.55 billion gain posted in April. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealers and\par analysts have said big changes in foreign reserves usually\par reflect the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  The Bank of Korea in a statement attributed the rise in\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par November to strength in non-dollar \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  -- which boosts\par dollar value of holdings in other units -- and investment gains.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Dealers in Seoul had earlier said South Korean authorities\par purchased about a combined $2 billion in two days of heavy\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  during November, and an additional unspecified\par amount for several other days during the month.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  South Korean foreign reserves have risen by 11 percent, or\par $23.87 billion, so far this year and have doubled in four years,\par Bank of Korea data shows. Its reserves rank behind those of\par China, Japan, Russia and Taiwan.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Senior officials at South Korea's finance ministry and\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have repeatedly voiced concerns that the won <KRW=>\par has overshot its fair value and that its sharp rise would hurt\par exports or export profitability at local companies.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  But recent trade figures appeared to belie their concerns as\par data on Friday showed that shipments abroad by Asia's\par third-largest economy jumped by a fifth in November from a year\par earlier, even at a time of a slowing U.S. economy.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  The commerce ministry said last Wednesday that exports for\par all of 2006 would grow 14.6 percent from last year, far outpacing\par its earlier projection of 11.8 percent growth.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  The Korea International Trade Association said on Sunday\par exports in 2007 would grow another 10.1 percent.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  South Korea's foreign reserves ($ billion, at end-month):  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Nov      Oct     Sept      Aug     July     June\par  234.26   229.46   228.22   227.02   225.72   224.36\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 KOREA-RESERVES/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061203e2c3001a4\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\ri